/* Question bank PA test (English convenience translation), Wft Basic. Vorm: [vraag, [[antwoord, uitleg] x4], toetsterm CDFD]; het EERSTE antwoord is steeds het juiste.
   Gegenereerd met tools/vragen-js.py. */
(window.PA_VRAGEN = window.PA_VRAGEN || {})["basis"] = [
["Which supervisory model does the Netherlands use for the financial sector?", [["Twin peaks: AFM supervises conduct, DNB prudential matters", "Supervision is divided by objective: the AFM looks at conduct towards clients and markets, DNB at the soundness of institutions."], ["A sectoral model with one supervisor per industry", "That model has in fact been abandoned; supervision is divided by objective and not by sector such as banks or insurers."], ["One central supervisor for the whole sector, namely DNB", "The Netherlands has two supervisors, each with its own task; DNB does not supervise the conduct of advisers."], ["Supervision by the Ministry of Finance, with the AFM and DNB as advisers", "The ministry makes policy and legislation; the supervision itself rests with the AFM and DNB."]], "1f.13"],
["Fatima Ouali (68) has just retired. Her AOW (state pension) and pension together are lower than her fixed costs and other expenses. She therefore takes €300.00 from her savings account every month to cover the shortfall. Her grandson calls this saving in reverse. What is what Fatima is doing called?", [["Dissaving", "In dissaving, previously accumulated wealth is used to pay for expenses that exceed income."], ["Borrowing", "Borrowing means using someone else's money that you have to repay; Fatima is using her own savings."], ["Investing in securities", "When investing in securities you deploy wealth to earn a return; Fatima is in fact drawing down wealth."], ["Capital investment", "Capital investment means spending money on means of production, such as a machine for a business."]], "1a.1"],
["According to the Wft, what is the purpose of the AFM's conduct supervision?", [["Orderly and transparent market processes, clean relationships between market parties and the careful treatment of clients", "This is the statutory description of conduct supervision; the emphasis is on the conduct of parties, including towards clients."], ["Safeguarding the financial soundness of banks, insurers and pension funds so that they can meet their obligations", "That is the purpose of prudential supervision, which is the task of DNB and not of the AFM."], ["Safeguarding the stability of the financial system as a whole and preventing crises", "Financial stability is one of DNB's tasks; the AFM focuses on conduct and transparency."], ["Settling individual disputes between consumers and financial service providers in a binding manner and awarding compensation", "Disputes are settled by Kifid or the court; the AFM is not a dispute resolution body."]], "1f.14"],
["Peter de Vries (52) took out a disability insurance policy through an adviser. At his first claim it turns out that the cover is narrower than he had understood. He angrily phones the AFM and expects the AFM to force the adviser to compensate him. He asks you whether this is the right route. What do you explain to Peter?", [["The AFM does not settle individual disputes; Peter submits his complaint to the adviser and can then go to Kifid", "The AFM uses reports as a signal for its supervision but does not award compensation. The internal complaints procedure and then Kifid or the court are intended for an individual dispute."], ["The AFM investigates the complaint, hears both parties and, if the complaint is well founded, awards compensation", "The AFM is a supervisor and not a dispute resolution body; compensation goes through Kifid or the court."], ["The AFM forwards the complaint to DNB, because DNB handles complaints about insurance", "DNB supervises prudential matters and likewise does not handle individual complaints from consumers."], ["The AFM obliges the adviser to reach a settlement with Peter within four weeks", "In an individual dispute the AFM cannot enforce a settlement; that is a matter for Kifid or the court."]], "1f.5"],
["Which measure can the AFM itself impose on a financial undertaking that infringes the Wft?", [["An administrative fine or a penalty order", "These are administrative-law enforcement instruments that the Wft grants to the AFM; in addition it can, among other things, issue a directive or withdraw the licence."], ["A prison sentence for the responsible directors", "Custodial sentences can only be imposed by the criminal court, not by a supervisor."], ["Compensation to the firm's prejudiced clients", "Awarding compensation is reserved for the court or a dispute resolution body such as Kifid."], ["Bankruptcy of the firm, declared by the AFM itself", "Bankruptcy is declared by the district court; the AFM cannot do this itself."]], "1f.17"],
["What is the best way for a consumer to check whether a financial adviser holds a Wft licence?", [["By consulting the AFM's public register", "The AFM grants the licences for advising and intermediation and keeps a public register of them."], ["By consulting the Chamber of Commerce's trade register", "Registration with the Chamber of Commerce says nothing about holding a Wft licence; every business must register there."], ["By requesting a licence check from the BKR (Dutch credit registration bureau)", "The BKR registers consumer credit and does not keep a register of licences."], ["By checking with DNB whether the firm is solvent", "DNB does not grant licences to advisers and intermediaries; the AFM does that."]], "1f.25"],
["To whom does the AFM grant a licence for advising on or intermediating in financial products?", [["To the financial undertaking", "The licence applies to the undertaking; individual employees must in addition be professionally qualified themselves."], ["To each individual adviser personally", "Employees do not need a licence of their own; the professional qualification requirements apply to them."], ["To the trade association on behalf of its members", "A trade association cannot hold a licence on behalf of members; each undertaking applies for its own."], ["To the provider, which thereby covers all its intermediaries", "The licence of a bank or insurer does not in principle cover the activities of independent intermediaries."]], "1f.25"],
["For which activity is a Wft licence from the AFM in principle required?", [["Advising on a term life insurance policy", "A term life insurance policy is a financial product within the meaning of the Wft; advising on it requires a licence."], ["Intermediating in the purchase of a home as an estate agent", "Estate agency in real property is not a service relating to a financial product within the meaning of the Wft."], ["Drawing up a will for a client", "A will is a notarial deed and not a financial product; no Wft licence applies to it."], ["Preparing the annual tax return", "Tax advice and filing work do not fall under the Wft licensing requirement."]], "1f.25"],
["What does the Wft essentially mean by intermediation?", [["Activities aimed at concluding an agreement on a financial product between client and provider", "Intermediation is about bringing about the agreement; for insurance it also includes assisting with its administration and performance."], ["Making a personal recommendation to a client about one or more specific financial products of a provider", "That is the description of advising; advising and intermediation are separate activities."], ["Entering into the agreement with the client oneself as the counterparty", "Whoever is the counterparty themselves offers the product; that is offering and not intermediation."], ["Managing the client's assets on their behalf at one's own discretion", "That is asset management, an investment service with its own regime."]], "1f.29"],
["A website explains in general terms the difference between an annuity mortgage and a linear mortgage, without asking the visitor for any details. Is this advising within the meaning of the Wft?", [["No, general information without a recommendation tailored to the person is not advice", "Without a personal recommendation about a specific product it is the provision of information, which must nevertheless be correct and not misleading."], ["Yes, all information about financial products counts as advice", "Not all information is advice; what matters is a personal recommendation about a specific product."], ["Yes, because information about mortgages is always licensable advice, even without client details", "General guidance may also be given about mortgages without it being advice."], ["No, because information on a website never falls under the Wft", "Advice can also be given online, and the Wft's information rules also apply to websites."]], "1f.19"],
["Ronald Bakker owns a bicycle shop and mainly sells electric bicycles costing around €3,000.00. At the till his employee offers customers a bicycle insurance policy against theft and damage. The shop says nothing about other insurance or financial products. Ronald wonders whether he has to apply for a Wft licence for this. What is correct?", [["This may fall under the exemption for insurance that is ancillary to the supply of goods", "The Wft Exemption Regulation contains an exemption for insurance that supplements the supply of goods, such as a bicycle. Ronald does have to check whether he meets all the conditions."], ["The shop always needs a full licence for intermediation in non-life insurance, just like an advisory firm", "There is in fact an exemption for insurance that is ancillary to the supply of goods."], ["The Wft does not apply, because the shop mainly sells bicycles and is not a financial undertaking", "Anyone who intermediates in insurance falls in principle under the Wft; the shop's main activity does not change that."], ["A licence is only needed if a customer expressly asks for advice about the insurance", "Intermediation without advice also requires a licence in principle; here the answer depends on the exemption."]], "1f.38"],
["A firm intermediates exclusively in personal non-life insurance and never gives advice in doing so. Does the firm need a Wft licence?", [["Yes, intermediation without advice also requires a licence in principle", "The Wft has a separate licensing requirement for intermediation, distinct from the one for advising."], ["No, only advising requires a licence", "Intermediation is an independent licensable activity alongside advising."], ["No, non-life insurance falls outside the Wft", "Non-life insurance policies are financial products within the meaning of the Wft."], ["Only if the premium per policy exceeds a statutory threshold of €1,000.00 per year", "The licensing requirement does not depend on the amount of the premium per policy."]], "1f.38"],
["Which requirement goes with obtaining and retaining an AFM licence as an adviser or intermediary?", [["The day-to-day policymakers must be reliable and suitable", "The AFM assesses the reliability and suitability of policymakers on the licence application and on changes."], ["The firm must be a member of a recognised trade association", "Membership of a trade association is voluntary and not a licensing requirement."], ["Every piece of advice must be approved in advance by the AFM", "The AFM supervises after the fact and does not approve individual advice."], ["The firm must work with a minimum of five providers per product type", "The Wft does not prescribe a minimum number of providers as a licensing requirement."]], "1f.33"],
["What is the consequence if a firm advises on mortgages without the required licence?", [["The firm infringes the Wft; the AFM can take enforcement action, for example with a fine or a penalty order", "Working without a licence is a breach of a core prohibition in the Wft, against which the AFM can take action."], ["The advice given is automatically void, so the client does not have to pay advice fees and the products taken out lapse", "The Wft does not provide that advice is automatically void; the civil-law consequences depend on the situation."], ["Kifid imposes a fine and removes the firm from the register", "Kifid is not a supervisor and does not impose fines; that is the AFM's power."], ["There is no consequence as long as the clients are satisfied with the advice", "Client satisfaction does not remove the breach of the licensing requirement."]], "1f.25"],
["Thijs (32) and Esra (30) live together in a home they own and both work full time. In three months they will have their first child. Afterwards Esra wants to work three days a week. They ask you what this new phase of life means for their financial overviews. Which change is the most to be expected?", [["Their expenses rise, for example because of childcare, while their income falls because Esra will work less", "A child brings additional fixed expenses, such as childcare and upkeep. If Esra works less, the household income falls at the same time."], ["Their expenses fall on balance, because they will eat out and go on holiday less often", "Some expenses may fall, but with a child fixed expenses usually rise."], ["Nothing changes, because the child benefit fully covers all the costs of a child", "Child benefit is a contribution and does not nearly cover all the costs of a child."], ["Their debts automatically become lower, because the mortgage interest rate falls when a family grows", "The mortgage interest rate does not depend on the growth of a family."]], "1a.3"],
["How is the professional qualification of an employee who advises on financial products built up?", [["A Wft diploma (Basic and the relevant product module), kept up to date through permanent education", "The diploma demonstrates the professional qualification and PE keeps that knowledge up to date."], ["A completed higher professional education degree in an economics field", "A general degree is not the same as a Wft diploma, unless it has been formally recognised as equivalent."], ["A minimum number of years of demonstrable work experience in the financial sector, recorded in an experience statement", "Work experience alone is no substitute for the required Wft diploma."], ["A certificate obtained once that remains valid for life", "The knowledge must be kept up to date; without PE the diploma does not remain valid."]], "1f.33"],
["An adviser does not pass his PE exam before the end of the applicable period. What is the consequence?", [["He no longer meets the qualification requirements and may not do that work until he does again", "Without current PE the professional qualification is no longer demonstrated, so the employee may not carry out those activities."], ["He automatically gets a year's extension without further consequences", "There is no automatic extension; failing to comply in time has immediate consequences for the professional qualification."], ["Only his employer receives a warning from the AFM; the adviser may simply keep working until the next PE period", "The employee himself may no longer advise; the employer must also monitor this."], ["He does not have to do anything as long as he has been advising for more than ten years", "Experience does not replace the PE obligation; it applies to everyone."]], "1f.33"],
["According to the Wft, who is responsible for ensuring that client-facing employees are professionally qualified?", [["The financial undertaking, which must ensure and demonstrate its employees' qualification", "The undertaking must ensure that the employees who carry out the activities are professionally qualified and must be able to demonstrate this."], ["Solely the employee, who must personally register their diploma and PE evidence with the AFM", "The employee must obtain the diploma and PE, but the undertaking is legally responsible for the professional qualification."], ["The AFM, which assesses every employee personally each year", "The AFM does not assess every employee; it supervises the undertaking."], ["The provider of the products being advised on", "A provider is not responsible for the professional qualification of the employees of an independent advisory firm."]], "1f.33"],
["Sanne (34) and Daan (36) have lived together in a rented house for eight years. They are not married, have no registered partnership and have not had a will drawn up. Daan has a substantial savings account in his own name. Sanne asks what happens to that money if Daan dies. What is correct?", [["Sanne does not inherit, because unmarried cohabitants without a will are not each other's heirs", "Statutory inheritance law recognises spouses and registered partners as heirs, but not unmarried cohabitants. Without a will, Daan's money goes to his family."], ["Sanne inherits everything, because they have lived together for more than five years", "The length of cohabitation does not confer inheritance rights; a will is needed for that."], ["Sanne inherits half, because cohabitants always have a right to an equal share", "Unmarried cohabitants have no statutory right to inherit from each other without a will."], ["Sanne only inherits if they have a cohabitation agreement together, even if there is no will", "A cohabitation agreement does not make Sanne a statutory heir; a will is needed for that."]], "1a.4"],
["Henk Brouwer (72) dies without a will. He was married to Truus (70) and had two children. Truus very much wants to stay living in their home. The children ask what statutory inheritance law means for them. What is correct according to the statutory division?", [["Truus receives the assets; the children receive a monetary claim on her that usually only becomes due on her death", "Under the statutory division the surviving spouse receives all the assets and the debts. The children receive a claim equal to the size of their share, which as a rule only becomes due on the death of the surviving spouse."], ["Truus and the children become joint owners of the house, so the children can demand that the house be sold", "The statutory division in fact protects the surviving spouse: the assets go to Truus."], ["The children receive everything, because Truus already has half of the assets through the marriage", "Truus is an heir alongside the children and receives the assets under the statutory division."], ["Without a will, Henk's estate passes to the State", "The State only inherits if there are no heirs; here there are a spouse and two children."]], "1a.5"],
["What is the essence of the general duty of care for financial service providers in the Wft?", [["Taking the client's legitimate interests carefully into account", "The general duty of care requires the service provider to take the client's legitimate interests carefully into account in providing services."], ["Selling as many products as possible within the statutory limits and one's own acceptance rules", "Turnover is not the focus; the duty of care is about the client's interest."], ["Informing the client only if they ask for it themselves", "The service provider must also provide relevant information of its own accord and act carefully."], ["Always guaranteeing the cheapest product on the market", "The duty of care requires a suitable solution, not necessarily the cheapest product."]], "1f.15"],
["Mark Jansen (38) has just become a father and wants to take out a term life insurance policy quickly. He asks adviser Linda for advice on the sum insured. When Linda asks about his income, his mortgage and his fixed costs, he does not want to say anything about them. He considers that private and just wants advice. What should Linda do?", [["Explain that she cannot give suitable advice without that information and otherwise refrain from advising", "An adviser must obtain information about the client's financial position and objectives. Without that information she cannot advise suitably and therefore gives no advice."], ["Advise anyway on the basis of average assumptions for a family with a child, without recording this", "Advice based on assumptions is not tailored to Mark and therefore not suitable; moreover the grounds must be recorded."], ["As a precaution, advise the highest possible cover so that the family will in any case have enough", "Excessive cover leads to an unnecessarily high premium and is likewise not suitable."], ["Have Mark sign a waiver and then advise on the basis of the information that is known", "A waiver does not release the adviser from the duty to advise suitably."]], "1f.19"],
["Why is it important that an adviser records the client profile and the grounds for their advice in the file?", [["So it can later be shown what the advice was based on and why it was suitable", "A good file makes the advice verifiable for the client, the firm and the supervisor."], ["Because otherwise the client does not have to pay the premium", "Recording the file has no effect on the client's payment obligation."], ["Because the file must be approved in advance by the AFM before the advice may be given to the client", "The AFM does not approve files in advance, but can request them during an investigation."], ["Because otherwise the provider may not issue the policy", "The provider has its own acceptance rules; the advice file is a duty of the adviser themselves."]], "2d.1"],
["With which four characteristics has the AFM described when a product or service puts the client's interest first?", [["Cost-efficient, useful, safe and understandable", "With these four characteristics the AFM has elaborated what putting the client's interest first means in practice."], ["Cheap, fast, digital and flexible", "These are desirable qualities, but not the characteristics the AFM uses."], ["Profitable, innovative, scalable and unique", "These are characteristics from the provider's perspective, not from the client's interest."], ["Independent, commission-free, guarantee-free and simple", "This combination is not the description the AFM uses."]], "4a.4"],
["What does the product development process (product approval and review process) require of providers of financial products?", [["Test products in advance against client interest, define a target group, review periodically", "Providers must design products in a balanced way for a particular target group and keep assessing them after launch."], ["That every new product is approved in advance by the AFM", "The AFM does not approve products in advance; the provider must have a careful process itself."], ["That they only test the profitability of the product", "The process is aimed at the client's interest and not only at profitability."], ["That products are only amended after Kifid has upheld complaints about the product or the AFM asks for it", "The process requires proactive testing in advance and periodically, not only after complaints."]], "1f.33"],
["What is the so-called special duty of care that has been developed in civil case law for financial institutions?", [["A duty, because of their expertise and social function, to protect the client, for example by warning of risks", "The Supreme Court developed this duty of care; it applies alongside the public-law Wft rules."], ["A Wft rule that applies exclusively to the largest systemically important banks and is enforced by the AFM with administrative fines", "The special duty of care comes from civil law and is not limited to large banks."], ["The client's duty to investigate all the risks of a financial product themselves before entering into an agreement, even after advice", "It is in fact a duty of the financial institution towards the client."], ["The AFM's duty to warn consumers personally", "The special duty of care rests on the institution, not on the supervisor."]], "1f.15"],
["Anouk Visser (29) wants to invest her savings in an aggressive equity fund, because a colleague is said to have earned a lot with it. Her adviser Bram establishes that she has little buffer and needs the money for a home in three years. He therefore expressly advises a more defensive solution. Anouk still wants the high-risk fund. What is the correct course of action for Bram?", [["He explains his advice and the risks clearly and records that Anouk is departing from it", "The client may depart from the advice. The adviser does make sure she understands the risks and records the advice and the departure."], ["He adapts his advice to her wish and records only that adapted advice in the file", "The file then does not match the actual advice and it can no longer be reconstructed what he advised."], ["He reports Anouk to the AFM, because she is making an irresponsible choice", "A client who departs from advice is not doing anything wrong; the AFM does not deal with such situations."], ["He arranges the desired fund without recording anything further, because it is her own choice", "Recording is especially necessary when departing from the advice, so that it is clear later what was advised."]], "1f.22"],
["What characterises execution-only services?", [["The client chooses without advice; no personal recommendation, but care is still required", "With execution only no advice is given, but the general duty of care and the information rules continue to apply."], ["No Wft rules apply, because no advice is given", "Even without advice, the duty of care and the information obligations, among others, apply."], ["The service provider remains liable for the suitability of the chosen product, just as in a full advisory process", "Without advice there is no advisory liability for suitability, although care remains necessary."], ["It is only permitted when opening a savings account", "Execution only occurs with more products; additional requirements apply to some of them."]], "1f.32"],
["What is the purpose of the services document (dienstverleningsdocument)?", [["To inform the client in advance of the nature and costs of the services and links with providers", "With this information the client can make a conscious choice whether, and from whom, to obtain advice or intermediation."], ["To inform the client about the policy conditions of the recommended product", "Product conditions come from the provider; the services document is about the firm's services."], ["To record in writing for the client the personal advice and its grounds, including the client profile", "That is done in the advice report, which is only drawn up after the fact-finding."], ["To inform the client annually about the value of their insurance policies", "A value statement is periodic product information, not information about the services."]], "1f.29"],
["When must the client in principle receive the information about the services and their costs?", [["Before the services begin", "The client must know in advance what to expect and what it costs, so that they can make a conscious choice about it."], ["When signing the provider's quotation", "By then the services have largely been provided and the client can no longer choose in advance."], ["After the services have ended, together with the invoice", "Informing about costs afterwards makes a conscious choice in advance impossible."], ["Only when the client expressly asks for it", "This is an obligation of the service provider, not information on request."]], "1f.3"],
["Under which conditions may an adviser call themselves independent?", [["If they advise on an analysis of enough market products and receive no commission from providers", "The term independent is protected; both a sufficiently broad market analysis and the absence of commission from providers are required."], ["If they are not employed by a bank or insurer", "Being self-employed is not enough; the statutory conditions concern market analysis and commission."], ["If they are a member of a professional association with its own code of conduct and are entered in that association's register", "Membership is not a statutory condition for using the term independent."], ["If they work with at least two providers", "Two providers is not necessarily a sufficient number, and the commission condition also applies."]], "1f.37"],
["Which standardised document must be provided under the IDD for a non-life insurance policy?", [["The insurance product information document (IPID)", "The IPID presents the essentials of a non-life insurance policy in a fixed format, such as the cover and exclusions."], ["The European Standardised Information Sheet (ESIS)", "The ESIS belongs to mortgage credit, not to non-life insurance."], ["The key information document under the PRIIPs Regulation", "This document applies to packaged investment products and insurance-based investment products, not to non-life insurance."], ["The standard European consumer credit information form", "This form belongs to consumer credit."]], "1f.3"],
["What is the ESIS?", [["A European Standardised Information Sheet with the main features and costs of a mortgage", "Thanks to its fixed structure the consumer can compare offers from different lenders."], ["A European test of the consumer's creditworthiness, which the lender must carry out before the offer", "The creditworthiness assessment is a separate obligation; the ESIS is an information document."], ["A register of all mortgages in the European Union", "There is no European mortgage register under this name; the ESIS is client information."], ["A European quality mark for sustainable mortgages", "The ESIS is not a quality mark but a mandatory information sheet."]], "1f.2"],
["What does the annual percentage rate of charge (APR) of a credit show?", [["The total cost of the credit to the consumer, as an annual percentage of the amount of credit", "In addition to interest, the APR includes other mandatory costs, so that credits are more easily comparable."], ["Only the nominal interest that the lender charges per year, excluding arrangement and intermediation costs", "The APR is broader than the nominal interest, because other costs are also included."], ["The part of the credit that must be repaid per year", "Repayment is the paying back of the principal and not a cost percentage."], ["The expected inflation over the term of the credit", "Inflation is not part of the APR."]], "1c.3"],
["Which warning sentence must be included in advertising for consumer credit?", [["Warning! Borrowing money costs money.", "This standard warning makes consumers aware that borrowing is not free."], ["Warning! Borrowing is always responsible.", "This is not a statutory text and would in fact be misleading."], ["Warning! You risk losing your investment.", "A warning like this fits investing, not credit advertising."], ["Warning! Consult the AFM first.", "This is not a prescribed text; the AFM does not give individual credit advice."]], "1c.10"],
["What does the commission ban entail?", [["Advisers and intermediaries may not receive commission from the provider for certain products; the client pays themselves", "For mortgages and complex products, among others, remuneration through the provider has been replaced by direct remuneration by the client."], ["Advisers may no longer receive any remuneration for any product; advice must henceforth be given free of charge by the provider", "Advisers may be paid, but then by the client themselves."], ["Providers may no longer build costs into their products", "The ban concerns commission to intermediaries, not all product costs."], ["Clients may no longer pay their adviser by the hour", "An hourly rate is in fact a common form of direct remuneration by the client."]], "1f.8"],
["Ria Smeets (63) wants to help her son Tim (27) with money for a buffer and a new car. She has heard that exemptions apply to gifts. Tim has never received a large gift from his mother. Ria asks what the difference is between the annual exemption and the one-off increased exemption. What is correct?", [["The annual exemption applies anew every year; Tim, as a child aged 18 to 40, can use the increased exemption once", "For a gift from parent to child an exemption applies every calendar year. A child aged 18 to 40 can use a higher exemption once, which replaces the ordinary exemption in that year."], ["The increased exemption may only be used for repaying the child's owner-occupied home debt", "That purpose belonged to the increased exemption for the owner-occupied home, which was abolished as of 2024."], ["There is no difference; both exemptions may be used in full by the child every year", "The increased exemption can only be used once."], ["The annual exemption only applies to gifts to children who are still younger than 18", "The annual exemption for children applies regardless of their age."]], "1a.6"],
["For which of the following products may an intermediary in principle receive commission from the provider?", [["A home contents insurance policy", "The commission ban does not apply to personal non-life insurance such as home contents insurance, although the remuneration must be transparent and balanced."], ["A mortgage credit", "The commission ban applies to mortgage credit."], ["A disability insurance policy for an individual", "Disability insurance policies fall under the commission ban."], ["An investment insurance policy", "An investment insurance policy is a complex product and falls under the commission ban."]], "1f.12"],
["What was an important reason for introducing the commission ban?", [["Removing the incentive to advise what pays most commission rather than what suits the client best", "Commission from the provider could steer the advice; direct remuneration makes the costs visible and the advice purer."], ["Lowering mortgage interest rates for all consumers", "The ban was not intended to lower interest rates, but to limit conflicts of interest."], ["Limiting the number of advisers in the Netherlands", "The aim was better quality of advice, not fewer advisers."], ["Enabling providers to employ more advisers themselves and sell their products directly to consumers", "The commission ban also applies to advice given by providers; the aim was to purify advice."]], "1f.8"],
["Sandra Mulder owns an advisory firm that advises on around two hundred mortgages a year. A lender phones her with an offer. If the firm places at least fifty mortgages with him this year, two advisers may go on a study trip to Lisbon free of charge. Sandra wonders whether she can accept. What is correct?", [["This is not permitted, because a benefit in kind from the provider also falls under the commission ban", "For mortgage credit an adviser may not receive commission from the provider, not even in kind. A trip that depends on the number of mortgages is moreover a strong incentive against the client's interest."], ["This is permitted, because it concerns a trip and not a sum of money", "The commission ban also applies to benefits in kind."], ["This is permitted, as long as the firm's clients pay nothing extra for it", "What matters is the incentive for the adviser, not what the client pays."], ["This is permitted if the firm clearly states the trip in the services document", "Transparency does not make a prohibited benefit permitted."]], "1f.8"],
["What applies to the remuneration of client-facing employees at a financial undertaking?", [["The remuneration must not create an incentive to act contrary to the client's interest", "Remuneration policy must be designed so that employees are not encouraged to sell products that are not in the client's interest."], ["The remuneration must depend entirely on the number of products sold, so that the firm's production rises", "Remuneration that is entirely production-linked in fact creates an incentive against the client's interest."], ["No rules apply, as long as the fixed salary is in line with the market", "Statutory rules also apply to variable remuneration and to remuneration policy."], ["Only directors fall under remuneration rules, not employees", "Remuneration rules also apply to employees, in particular to those who work with clients."]], "1f.12"],
["What is the correct approach to conflicts of interest under the regulations?", [["Identify conflicts of interest, prevent or manage them, and inform the client if that is insufficient", "Disclosing to the client is the last resort; the undertaking must first prevent or manage the conflict itself."], ["Mention conflicts of interest only in the general terms and conditions, so that the client agrees to them on signing", "A general mention is not management of the specific conflict."], ["Disclose conflicts of interest only if the client asks about them", "The undertaking must itself actively identify and address conflicts of interest."], ["Conflicts of interest are permitted as long as the AFM does not ask about them", "There is a separate obligation to manage conflicts of interest, independent of any questions from the AFM."]], "4a.4"],
["Rob Hendriks is an independent mortgage adviser. In a private capacity he owns a sizeable shareholding in a small lender, on whose mortgages he also regularly advises. His client Jeroen receives advice from Rob to borrow from precisely this lender. Jeroen knows nothing about Rob's shares. What is correct?", [["There is a conflict of interest that Rob must manage and about which he must clearly inform Jeroen", "Rob's own financial interest may influence his advice. He must manage that conflict and, if that is not enough, clearly inform Jeroen about it in advance."], ["There is no problem, because the shares are private property and fall outside his business", "A private interest can also influence the advice and is therefore a conflict of interest."], ["Rob may never again advise on this lender, even if that is best for the client", "A conflict of interest must be managed and disclosed; an absolute ban does not follow from it."], ["It is only relevant if Jeroen himself holds shares in this lender", "What matters is the adviser's interest, not the client's."]], "4a.4"],
["Adviser Fatma Yilmaz has had the Bos family as clients for years. The family is selling its home to the young couple Kevin and Iris. Kevin and Iris ask Fatma to arrange their mortgage, while the Bos family asks her to help think about the financial settlement of the sale. Fatma wonders whether she can accept both assignments. What is correct?", [["There is a conflict of interest, because the interests of buyer and seller may be opposed", "Buyer and seller, for example, have opposing interests regarding price and conditions. Fatma must prevent or manage this conflict and, if necessary, can decline one of the assignments."], ["There is no conflict of interest, because it concerns one and the same home", "Precisely because it concerns the same transaction, the interests may clash."], ["There is no conflict of interest as long as both parties are satisfied with the outcome", "A conflict of interest does not depend on satisfaction afterwards, but on opposing interests in advance."], ["There is only a conflict of interest if Fatma also acts as estate agent in the sale", "Even without an estate agent role, advising both sides can lead to a conflict of interest."]], "4a.4"],
["What must a financial undertaking record with regard to conflicts of interest?", [["A conflicts of interest policy and a register of situations in which they have arisen or may arise", "Recording makes the management of conflicts of interest verifiable for the undertaking and the supervisor."], ["Only the conflicts of interest that have led to a complaint", "Conflicts without a complaint must also be identified and managed."], ["Nothing, because conflicts of interest are discussed solely orally with the client concerned and the compliance officer", "Discussing them orally is insufficient; the policy and the register must be demonstrable."], ["Only conflicts of interest of directors, not of employees", "Employees can also have conflicts of interest that need to be managed."]], "1f.33"],
["What must a consumer do before they can take a complaint to Kifid?", [["First submit the complaint to the financial service provider itself", "Kifid only handles a complaint once the service provider's internal complaints procedure has not led to a solution."], ["First start proceedings before the subdistrict court judge", "Kifid is in fact an alternative to the court; legal proceedings in advance are not necessary."], ["First ask the AFM for permission", "The AFM plays no role in access to Kifid."], ["First engage a lawyer who submits the complaint in writing on their behalf", "A consumer can submit a complaint themselves; a lawyer is not mandatory."]], "1f.5"],
["Kevin de Bruin (29) has debts to six creditors, including a credit card and arrears with his health insurer. He can no longer keep up with the payments and is receiving more and more reminders. He asks the bank what he can do. He has heard of debt restructuring through the court. What do you explain to him in outline?", [["He can request debt assistance through the municipality; if an amicable arrangement fails, the court can admit him to the Wsnp", "First an attempt is made to reach an amicable arrangement with all creditors, for example through municipal debt assistance. If that fails, he can ask the court for admission to the statutory debt restructuring scheme (Wsnp)."], ["He can apply directly to the AFM for debt restructuring, which immediately cancels his debts", "The AFM is a supervisor and does not arrange debt restructuring for consumers."], ["He can ask the BKR to have his debts lapse and his registrations removed", "The BKR registers credit and arrears, but does not cancel debts."], ["He can consolidate his debts into a new revolving credit, with which the restructuring starts automatically", "Consolidation is not debt restructuring and can worsen his situation; with problematic debts, debt assistance is the appropriate route."]], "1a.12"],
["A consumer has received a non-binding ruling from Kifid and does not agree with it. What can they do?", [["They can still put the case before the court", "A non-binding ruling is advice; the parties can then go to court."], ["Nothing, every Kifid ruling is final", "Only a binding ruling binds the parties; a non-binding ruling does not."], ["They must ask the AFM to review the ruling", "The AFM has no power to review Kifid rulings."], ["They can only submit a new complaint to the same committee", "Submitting the same complaint again is not a usual route; the court is open to them."]], "1f.21"],
["What is part of careful internal complaint handling by an advisory firm?", [["Registering complaints, answering promptly and substantively, and analysing them to prevent repeats", "A good procedure resolves the complaint and uses the lesson to improve the services."], ["Handling complaints only if they are submitted by registered letter and within six weeks of the advice", "A threshold like this does not fit an accessible complaints procedure."], ["Forwarding complaints straight to Kifid without a response of its own", "The firm must first handle the complaint itself."], ["Registering complaints only when the client demands compensation", "Complaints without a damages claim must also be registered and handled."]], "3c.1"],
["Mr Van Dam phones the firm. He has been waiting for three weeks for the promised quotation for his home contents and buildings insurance and is very angry about it. He says he cannot be bothered to write a letter as well and hangs up. Your colleague thinks this is not a complaint, because nothing is on paper. What is correct?", [["This is a complaint that must be handled and registered in accordance with the complaints procedure", "An oral expression of dissatisfaction is also a complaint. It is recorded and dealt with, for example by calling Mr Van Dam back."], ["This is not a complaint, because only written complaints count in the register", "A complaint does not have to be in writing to be handled as a complaint."], ["This is a matter for Kifid, so the firm does not have to do anything itself", "A complaint is first handled by the service provider itself; Kifid comes only afterwards."], ["This is only a complaint if Mr Van Dam can demonstrably show he has suffered financial loss", "Dissatisfaction with the services is already a complaint, even without loss."]], "3c.1"],
["What does customer due diligence under the Wwft consist of?", [["Identifying and verifying customer and UBO, determining purpose and nature of the relationship, ongoing monitoring", "Customer due diligence is more than an identity check: the purpose of the relationship and continuous monitoring are also part of it."], ["Only copying the customer's identity document", "Identification is just one component; verification, UBO, purpose and monitoring are also needed."], ["A credit check with the BKR and an income assessment", "These are creditworthiness checks, not components of Wwft customer due diligence."], ["Requesting a certificate of conduct for the customer and a recent extract from the Personal Records Database (BRP)", "A certificate of conduct and a BRP extract are not components of customer due diligence under the Wwft."]], "2b.1"],
["With which body does an undertaking subject to the Wwft report an unusual transaction?", [["FIU-Nederland", "The Financial Intelligence Unit receives and analyses reports of unusual transactions."], ["The police", "The report goes to FIU-Nederland, which passes on data to investigating authorities where necessary."], ["The AFM", "The AFM supervises compliance but is not the reporting point for unusual transactions."], ["The Tax and Customs Administration", "The Tax and Customs Administration is not the reporting point under the Wwft."]], "4a.3"],
["Adviser Joyce reported an unusual transaction by her client Arjen Kok to FIU-Nederland last month. Arjen had paid a large single premium for an annuity from an unclear source. Now he phones her. He has a feeling that something is not right and asks whether anything is going on with his file. What may Joyce say?", [["She may not tell him that a report has been made", "A duty of confidentiality applies to a report: the client may not find out that they have been reported. Joyce therefore keeps the conversation neutral."], ["She must inform Arjen fully about the report and the reason for it", "That is contrary to the duty of confidentiality surrounding reports."], ["She may tell him if Arjen asks in writing to inspect his file", "A request for access also does not override the duty of confidentiality surrounding a report."], ["She may tell him, because the transaction has already been carried out", "The duty of confidentiality continues to apply even after the transaction has been carried out."]], "4a.3"],
["Hanneke Vermeulen, as a new client, wants to pay a large single premium for an annuity insurance policy. Customer due diligence shows that she is a member of the House of Representatives. Her file otherwise looks in order. Your colleague thinks she is simply a client like any other. What is correct?", [["Enhanced customer due diligence, including into the source of her wealth, with approval at a higher level", "A member of the House of Representatives is a politically exposed person. Enhanced measures then apply, such as an investigation into the source of wealth and approval by senior management."], ["The firm may not enter into a business relationship with a politically exposed person", "A relationship with a PEP is permitted, but requires enhanced measures."], ["The same measures apply as for any other client, because her file is in order", "For a PEP the Wwft prescribes enhanced customer due diligence."], ["The firm must first report her to FIU-Nederland and wait for permission", "PEP status is not in itself an unusual transaction, and FIU-Nederland does not give permission in advance."]], "2b.1"],
["How long must data from customer due diligence under the Wwft be retained at a minimum?", [["Five years after the end of the business relationship or after the transaction has been carried out", "The Wwft prescribes this period so that data are available for investigation."], ["Seven years after the business relationship was entered into, equal to the tax retention obligation for records", "Seven years is the tax retention obligation; the Wwft uses a different period and a different starting point."], ["One year after the last transaction", "That period is too short for the Wwft."], ["For as long as the client consents to it", "The retention obligation is statutory and does not depend on the client's consent."]], "2d.1"],
["What protects a reporter who reports an unusual transaction in good faith?", [["They are exempt from criminal and civil liability for the report", "The Wwft protects the reporter acting in good faith, so that the reporting obligation does not lead to liability."], ["They receive a financial reward from FIU-Nederland", "There is no reward for a report."], ["They automatically receive a new identity", "That is not part of the Wwft scheme."], ["They are not protected and themselves bear the risk of a damages claim from the client they reported", "The Wwft in fact offers protection to reporters acting in good faith."]], "4a.3"],
["Erik Smits approaches the firm on behalf of a holding company (BV) for a life insurance policy that the company wants to take out for its director. When asked who the company's ultimate beneficial owners are, he is evasive. He says the shareholders would rather remain anonymous. Even after further questioning you get no clarity. What must the firm do?", [["Not enter into a relationship, because customer due diligence cannot be completed, and consider making a report", "If the UBO cannot be established, the relationship may not be entered into. The refusal can moreover be a reason to report an unusual transaction."], ["Enter into the relationship and complete the UBO investigation later, once the policy is running", "Customer due diligence must in principle be completed before the relationship begins."], ["Enter into the relationship if Erik declares that he is himself the sole director of the company", "Being a director says nothing about who the ultimate beneficial owners are."], ["Enter into the relationship, because the UBO obligation only applies to banks and trust offices", "An intermediary subject to the Wwft must also establish the UBO."]], "1b.3"],
["On what basis does an adviser usually process a client's income data in order to give mortgage advice?", [["The processing is necessary for the performance of the contract with the client", "Without income data the requested advice cannot be given; this is a basis in its own right alongside consent."], ["The client's consent is always required and is the only possible basis for financial data", "The GDPR (AVG) recognises six lawful bases; consent is one of them and is not always the most appropriate."], ["The vital interest of the client", "This basis is intended for life-threatening situations, not for advice."], ["The general interest of a well-functioning mortgage market", "This basis applies to tasks carried out in the public interest, not to advice to a client."]], "1f.40"],
["After a client visit, adviser Tim leaves his laptop on the train. The laptop holds unencrypted files on some sixty clients, with income data and copies of passports. The laptop is not recovered. Tim would rather keep the incident quiet. What must the firm do?", [["Report the data breach in principle within 72 hours to the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens) and, where necessary, inform the clients", "A data breach that poses a risk to the individuals concerned must in principle be reported to the AP within 72 hours. In the case of a high risk, as here with passport copies, the clients are also informed."], ["Only record the breach internally, because it was a mishap by a single employee", "Unintended loss is also a data breach; with this risk it must be reported to the AP."], ["Report the breach within 72 hours to the AFM, because it concerns clients' financial data", "Data breaches are reported to the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens, not to the AFM."], ["Wait to see whether a client reports damage and only then take action", "The reporting obligation does not depend on a complaint or reported damage."]], "4a.5"],
["Which of the following data is special category personal data under the GDPR (AVG)?", [["Information about the client's health", "Health data are special category personal data; processing is in principle prohibited except under specific exceptions."], ["The client's gross annual income and wealth position", "Income and wealth are sensitive, but not special category personal data within the meaning of the GDPR (AVG)."], ["The client's home address", "An address is ordinary personal data."], ["The client's email address", "An email address is ordinary personal data."]], "1f.40"],
["A client asks the firm what personal data it holds about them. What applies?", [["The client has a right of access and the firm must in principle respond within one month", "The GDPR (AVG) gives a right of access; the period can be extended for complex requests."], ["The firm only has to respond if the client engages a lawyer", "The client can exercise the right of access themselves."], ["The firm may always refuse an access request on grounds of trade secrets or internal advice notes", "Refusal is possible only in exceptional cases; the right of access is the starting point."], ["The firm must first submit the data to the AFM", "The AFM plays no role in access requests under the GDPR (AVG)."]], "1f.39"],
["May an adviser simply use data obtained for mortgage advice for a marketing campaign by a partner company?", [["No, data may only be used for compatible purposes; for a different purpose a basis of its own is needed", "The principle of purpose limitation prevents data from being used unnoticed for new purposes."], ["Yes, once data have been obtained they may be used freely", "The GDPR (AVG) has purpose limitation; free use is not permitted."], ["Yes, if the partner company is also a financial undertaking with its own AFM licence and a published privacy statement", "The type of recipient does not change the requirement of an appropriate basis."], ["Yes, if the client does not object within a week", "Silence does not count as consent under the GDPR (AVG)."]], "4a.5"],
["A firm has its client files stored by an external software supplier. What is correct?", [["The firm must conclude a data processing agreement and remains the controller", "The supplier processes data on instruction and is a processor; the firm remains responsible."], ["The supplier automatically becomes the sole controller", "The firm determines the purpose and means and remains responsible."], ["No agreements are needed, because the supplier must itself comply with the GDPR (AVG) and is itself liable for that", "The GDPR (AVG) in fact requires written agreements with a processor."], ["Only the consent of each client is required", "This is a processor relationship, which requires an agreement and not consent."]], "4a.5"],
["Who must take the oath or affirmation for the financial sector?", [["Not only directors, but also employees of a financial undertaking in the Netherlands, for example those with client contact", "The oath or affirmation applies to directors and supervisory directors and also to many employees, such as those who work directly with clients."], ["Exclusively directors and supervisory directors of banks and insurers that are under DNB's prudential supervision", "The obligation is broader and also applies to employees, and not only at banks."], ["Only advisers who are self-employed entrepreneurs", "The oath is not limited to the self-employed; employees are covered by it too."], ["Only employees who have had a criminal record", "The oath is a general integrity declaration and does not depend on the employee's past."]], "4a.4"],
["What is the purport of the oath or affirmation for the financial sector?", [["Acting with integrity and care, putting the client's interest first and promoting trust in the financial sector", "The oath underlines employees' personal responsibility for a sector with integrity."], ["The promise to maximise the employer's profit as far as possible and inform the shareholders about it annually", "The oath is not about profit, but about integrity and the client's interest."], ["The promise never to make a mistake in advice", "Mistakes are human; the oath is about acting with integrity and care."], ["The promise to offer only the products of one's own employer", "The oath contains no product preference; the client's interest is central."]], "4a.4"],
["Lisa (28) and Ahmed (30) are moving in together and open an and/or account together for the fixed costs. Lisa asks what this means for the money in the account. Ahmed wants to know who is liable if the account is overdrawn. They ask you for an explanation. What is correct?", [["Each can operate the account independently and both are jointly and severally liable for a shortfall", "With an and/or account each account holder may withdraw or transfer money without the other. If the account is overdrawn, the bank can recover the entire shortfall from either of them."], ["Only both together can make a payment, and each is liable for half", "That resembles an and account; with an and/or account each can operate it independently and each is liable for the whole."], ["Each can operate it independently, but only the first account holder is liable", "With an and/or account both account holders are jointly and severally liable."], ["The balance belongs half to each, so the bank refuses withdrawals above that half", "The bank does not check who withdraws which part; each may operate the account independently."]], "1b.1"],
["What is meant by an integrity risk for a financial undertaking?", [["Risk of damage to reputation or capital from unethical conduct, such as fraud or money laundering", "Integrity in business operations requires the undertaking to analyse and manage these risks."], ["The risk that the interest rate on the capital market rises", "That is a market risk, not an integrity risk."], ["The risk that a client does not pay their premium on time", "That is a credit risk, not an integrity risk."], ["The risk that the firm's software becomes outdated and client data consequently become inaccessible", "That is an operational or IT risk, not an integrity risk in the proper sense."]], "4a.3"],
["First-time buyers Sem and Julia want to buy an apartment, but their income is just too low for the mortgage they want. Your colleague Patrick suggests entering a few hundred euros more income in the application than stated on the employer's statement. According to him nobody is worse off for it. Sem and Julia know nothing about it. What is the correct response?", [["Not cooperate and report the incident internally, for example to compliance or the line manager", "Stating too high an income is fraud and may cause the clients financial problems. You do not cooperate and report it in accordance with the internal procedure."], ["Cooperate, because that way Sem and Julia can still buy the apartment", "Fraud is never in the client's interest; they get a loan that they may not be able to afford."], ["Cooperate, as long as the difference is only a few hundred euros", "The size makes no difference; even a small adjustment is fraud."], ["Do nothing and leave it to the lender to check the data", "Looking the other way does not fit acting with integrity; you must report the incident."]], "4a.3"],
["What characterises an annuity loan at a constant interest rate?", [["Constant gross monthly payment; the interest part falls, the repayment part rises", "With an annuity, the composition of the fixed instalment gradually shifts from interest to repayment."], ["The same amount is repaid every month, so the gross monthly payment falls over time", "This is the characteristic of a linear loan."], ["Repayment is made in one go only at the end of the term", "This characterises an interest-only loan."], ["The interest portion stays the same and the repayment portion falls", "The interest portion in fact falls, because the debt keeps getting smaller."]], "1c.23"],
["Ilse and Ruben borrow €200,000.00 for their home, with a term of 30 years and a fixed interest rate for the whole term. They are torn between annuity and linear repayment. Ilse wants the lowest possible monthly payment at the start. Ruben wants to pay as little interest as possible over the whole term. Which statement is correct?", [["Linear gives less interest in total, but annuity gives a lower gross monthly payment at the start", "With linear, repayment is faster from the start, so the debt and the interest fall faster. The gross monthly payment is therefore higher at the start than with annuity."], ["Annuity gives less interest in total and also the lowest gross monthly payment at the start", "With annuity, less is repaid at the start, so in fact more interest is paid over the whole term."], ["Both forms lead to the same total interest, because the amount and the term are the same", "Total interest depends on how fast the debt falls, and that differs per repayment form."], ["Linear gives less interest in total and also the lowest gross monthly payment at the start", "With linear, the first monthly payment is in fact the highest, because a fixed amount is repaid from the start."]], "1c.23"],
["Noor (24) has just started her first job and puts €2,000.00 into a savings account with interest of 5% per year. She leaves the money for two years and withdraws nothing. The interest is credited every year and then earns interest itself. She asks you what will be in her account after two years. What is the correct amount?", [["€2,205.00", "After one year there is €2,100.00. In the second year 5% on €2,100.00 is added, i.e. €105.00, making €2,205.00 in total."], ["€2,200.00", "That is simple interest; the interest on the first year's interest is missing."], ["€2,100.00", "That is the balance after one year, not after two years."], ["€2,250.00", "This amount is too high; at 5% per year, €205.00 is added in two years."]], "2a.1"],
["The savings rate is 2% and inflation is 3%. What happens to the purchasing power of the savings, disregarding taxes?", [["The purchasing power falls, because prices rise faster than the savings balance grows", "The real return is negative; after a year less can be bought with the balance."], ["The purchasing power rises, because interest is credited", "The nominal growth is lower than the price increase, so purchasing power does not rise."], ["The purchasing power stays the same, because interest and inflation cancel each other out over a full year", "Interest and inflation are not equal here; inflation is higher."], ["The purchasing power depends only on the size of the balance", "Purchasing power is determined by the relationship between the balance and the price level."]], "1b.15"],
["Wim Peters (71) has €80,000.00 in a savings account and €40,000.00 in a current account, both with bank A. In addition he has €30,000.00 in a savings account with bank B, a different bank with its own licence. Bank A goes bankrupt. Wim wonders how much of his money is protected. How much of his balance with bank A does he get back via the deposit guarantee scheme?", [["€100,000.00", "The deposit guarantee scheme protects €100,000.00 per account holder per bank, for all accounts with that bank combined. Of the €120,000.00 with bank A, €20,000.00 is therefore not covered."], ["€120,000.00", "The cover applies per account holder per bank, not per account; above €100,000.00 there is no guarantee."], ["€80,000.00", "Balances in a current account also fall under the deposit guarantee scheme."], ["€70,000.00", "The balance with bank B does not count; that bank has not failed and falls under its own cover."]], "1b.21"],
["What does the indemnity principle mean for non-life insurance?", [["The payout is no higher than the loss actually suffered; the insured may not end up better off", "A non-life insurance policy compensates the loss and is not intended to make a profit."], ["The insurer always pays out the sum insured, regardless of the loss", "That characterises a sum-assured insurance policy, not a non-life insurance policy."], ["The insured may claim the same loss in full from several insurers, provided they pay each policy themselves", "Double compensation would enrich the insured, which the principle in fact excludes."], ["The premium is determined afterwards on the basis of the loss", "The principle is about the payout, not about setting the premium."]], "1g.15"],
["Annelies and Koen have lived in the same house for twenty years and have never adjusted their home contents insurance in all that time. The contents are insured for €30,000.00, but after a fire turn out to be worth €60,000.00. The fire causes €10,000.00 of damage. Their policy has no guarantee against underinsurance. What does the insurer pay out under the proportionality rule?", [["€5,000.00", "Insurance is for half of the actual value, so the loss is compensated at half: €10,000.00 x 30,000/60,000."], ["€10,000.00", "Without a guarantee against underinsurance, the loss is not fully compensated in the event of underinsurance."], ["€30,000.00", "The sum insured is a maximum, not a payout for every loss."], ["€3,333.33", "This calculation does not apply the ratio correctly; the ratio of insured to value is 1/2."]], "1g.16"],
["In which box of income tax does an individual's savings fall?", [["Box 3", "Box 3 taxes income from savings and investments."], ["Box 1", "Box 1 concerns income from work and home, such as salary and the owner-occupied home."], ["Box 2", "Box 2 concerns income from a substantial interest in a company."], ["Savings fall outside income tax", "Savings can be taxed in box 3, depending on the wealth and the tax-free allowance."]], "1a.8"],
["What repayment requirement must a new mortgage loan for the owner-occupied home in principle meet, since 2013, for the interest to be deductible?", [["At least annuity repayment of the loan within a maximum of 30 years", "For new owner-occupied home debts since 1 January 2013, mortgage interest deduction is linked to this repayment requirement."], ["The loan may be interest-only if the client holds a savings account", "A new interest-only loan does not meet the repayment requirement for interest deduction."], ["The loan must be fully repaid within ten years", "The law does not require repayment within ten years, but at least on an annuity basis within a maximum of 30 years."], ["No repayment requirement applies, as long as the home is the main residence", "Main residence is a condition for the owner-occupied home, but the repayment requirement also applies."]], "1c.23"],
["What is the difference between a personal loan and a revolving credit?", [["Personal loan: fixed amount and fixed term; revolving credit: drawing and repaying within a limit", "These are the core characteristics of the two forms of consumer credit."], ["A personal loan always has a variable interest rate; a revolving credit in fact always has a fixed rate", "It is usually the other way round: a revolving credit usually has a variable interest rate."], ["With a revolving credit nothing ever has to be repaid", "With a revolving credit an instalment is also paid monthly."], ["A personal loan is not registered, a revolving credit is", "Both forms of credit are in principle registered with the BKR."]], "1c.5"],
["What does the Central Credit Information System (CKI) of the BKR register?", [["Consumer credit and any payment arrears on it", "Lenders consult this register to prevent over-borrowing."], ["The wealth that consumers hold in their savings and investment accounts at banks", "Savings balances are not registered with the BKR."], ["All insurance policies of consumers", "Insurance policies are not registered in the CKI."], ["Consumers' income according to the Tax and Customs Administration", "Income data are not part of the CKI."]], "1a.10"],
["What is the difference between a tax credit and a deduction in income tax?", [["A tax credit reduces the tax payable itself; a deduction reduces taxable income", "A deduction yields a benefit at the tax rate, whereas a tax credit is deducted directly from the tax."], ["A tax credit reduces taxable income; a deduction directly reduces the tax payable itself", "This is exactly the wrong way round."], ["There is no difference; both terms mean the same", "Both operate at a different level in the tax calculation."], ["A tax credit applies only to entrepreneurs", "Tax credits, such as the general tax credit, also apply to individuals."]], "1a.8"],
["What type of obligation does an adviser as a rule have under the contract for services?", [["An obligation of best efforts: they must observe the care of a good contractor", "The adviser promises to work carefully, not to achieve a particular result such as a guaranteed return."], ["An obligation to achieve a result: they guarantee that the recommended product delivers the intended result", "An adviser does not as a rule guarantee an outcome; they must act carefully."], ["An obligation to do only what the client literally asks", "A good contractor thinks along and warns where necessary."], ["No obligation, because advice is non-binding", "An advisory assignment is a contract from which obligations arise."]], "1f.29"],
["What must a creditor as a rule do before the debtor is in default for failing to perform a contract?", [["Give the debtor notice of default with a reasonable period in which to perform after all", "Default only occurs after that period has expired, unless an exception applies such as a strict deadline."], ["Immediately ask the court to dissolve the contract", "Dissolution as a rule first requires default, and can also take place out of court."], ["Report the debtor to the AFM", "The AFM plays no role in civil-law performance."], ["Nothing; default always arises automatically on the day on which the agreed performance should have taken place", "Automatic default applies only in exceptional cases, such as with a strict deadline."]], "1c.8"],
["When does a client's claim for damages against their adviser as a rule become time-barred?", [["Five years after becoming aware of the damage and the liable person, and at the latest twenty years after the event that caused the damage", "This is the main rule in the Dutch Civil Code (BW) for the limitation of damages claims."], ["One year after the advice was given, regardless of when the client discovers the damage or the error", "A period of one year is not the main rule for damages claims."], ["Never; a claim against an adviser is not subject to limitation", "Claims against advisers are also subject to limitation."], ["Three months after the first complaint to the adviser, unless the client starts proceedings with Kifid within that period", "This period has nothing to do with civil-law limitation."]], "1f.5"],
["Youssef El Amrani (26) takes out a car insurance policy through an intermediary. The application form asks about claims in the past five years. Youssef states that he has had no claims, although last year he made two claims with another insurer. He thinks the new insurer will not see that anyway. What applies to Youssef's duty of disclosure?", [["He must disclose facts that he knows and that he should understand are important to the insurer", "His claims history is such a fact, and it is also asked about. If he conceals it, the insurer can pay out less or nothing on a claim and, in the case of intent to mislead, terminate the insurance."], ["He only has to disclose facts that the insurer requests from him after a first claim", "The duty of disclosure applies in fact before the insurance is taken out."], ["He does not have to disclose anything; the insurer must investigate his claims history itself", "The insurer may rely on the client disclosing the requested facts correctly."], ["He only has to disclose claims made with the same insurer", "Claims with another insurer are also relevant for assessing the risk."]], "1g.12"],
["Lotte de Graaf (31) takes out a home contents insurance policy on a Sunday evening via an insurer's website. She has spoken to no one and filled everything in digitally. Two days later she sees a cheaper policy with wider cover elsewhere. She wants to undo the insurance she has just taken out. What right does Lotte have in principle?", [["She can withdraw from the contract within 14 days without giving reasons", "For a financial service concluded at a distance, the consumer has in principle a 14-day cooling-off period. Lotte is well within it."], ["She has no right of withdrawal, because the cover started immediately", "The right of withdrawal also applies if the cover has already started."], ["She can only withdraw on the day of taking out the policy, not afterwards", "The statutory cooling-off period is 14 days, not one day."], ["She can only cancel at the end of the first insurance year", "Thanks to the right of withdrawal she does not have to wait until the end of the contract year."]], "1g.21"],
["What applies to a term in general terms and conditions that is on the black list in a consumer contract?", [["The term is always regarded as unreasonably onerous and is voidable", "With the black list no further weighing is needed; with the grey list unreasonableness is only presumed."], ["The term is presumed to be unreasonably onerous, but evidence to the contrary is possible", "This is the characteristic of the grey list."], ["The term is always valid, because the consumer has signed", "Signing does not make a black-list term valid."], ["The term applies only between businesses, not towards consumers", "The black list is in fact intended to protect consumers."]], "1g.1"],
["An employee of an advisory firm makes a mistake in the advice, as a result of which the client suffers loss. Against whom can the client as a rule recover the loss?", [["The advisory firm, which is the contracting party and is liable as employer for its employees", "The client concluded the contract with the firm; employer's liability for the mistakes of employees also applies."], ["Only against the employee personally", "The client can as a rule hold the firm liable; the employee's personal liability is limited."], ["The AFM, because it supervises the firm", "The supervisor is not liable for a firm's advisory errors."], ["The provider of the recommended product, because it issued the policy and receives the premium", "The provider is not responsible for the mistakes of an independent advisory firm."]], "1f.35"],
["Which of the following schemes is an employee insurance?", [["The WIA", "The WIA (Work and Income according to Labour Capacity Act) is an employee insurance for long-term incapacity for work, financed by premiums through the employer."], ["The AOW (state pension)", "The AOW is a national insurance for everyone who lives or works in the Netherlands."], ["The Anw (Surviving Dependants Act)", "The Anw is a national insurance for surviving dependants."], ["The Long-term Care Act (Wlz)", "The Wlz is a national insurance for long-term care."]], "1d.7"],
["Karin Boer (45) works as a nurse in a hospital. After a serious accident she has been fully off sick for a year. Her employer continues to pay her salary and her reintegration is being worked on hard. Karin wonders when she can receive a WIA benefit if she does not recover. When can a WIA benefit as a rule start?", [["After 104 weeks of illness", "The WIA has a waiting period of 104 weeks, during which the employer continues to pay the salary. Only in the case of permanent total incapacity for work can an IVA benefit sometimes start earlier."], ["After 13 weeks of illness, when the employer stops paying", "The employer does not stop after 13 weeks; salary continuation goes on and a WIA benefit does not yet follow."], ["Immediately on the first day of illness", "In the first two years the employer continues to pay the salary."], ["After 52 weeks of illness", "After a year of illness the WIA waiting period runs for another year."]], "1d.9"],
["When is someone entitled to an IVA benefit within the WIA?", [["If they are fully and permanently incapacitated for work", "The IVA is intended for those who have no or hardly any chance of recovery and are fully incapacitated for work."], ["If they are partially incapacitated for work and have a chance of recovery", "In that situation the WGA applies, not the IVA."], ["If they are less than 35% incapacitated for work", "With less than 35% incapacity for work there is in principle no entitlement to a WIA benefit."], ["If they have become unemployed after a reorganisation", "Unemployment falls under the WW (unemployment benefit), not the IVA."]], "1d.13"],
["Ahmed Bakkali (50) is a warehouse employee and, after a slipped disc, has not been able to work fully for two years. At the WIA assessment, UWV (Employee Insurance Agency) establishes that he is 25% incapacitated for work. He can still do other suitable work. Ahmed asks what this means for a benefit under the WIA. What applies in principle?", [["No entitlement to a WIA benefit, because he is less than 35% incapacitated for work", "With less than 35% incapacity for work there is in principle no entitlement to a WIA benefit. Ahmed remains reliant on income from (other) work."], ["He receives an IVA benefit for the duration of his incapacity for work", "The IVA is only for those fully and permanently incapacitated for work."], ["He receives a WGA benefit in proportion to his 25% incapacity for work", "The WGA only applies from 35% incapacity for work."], ["Until his AOW age he receives a supplement through the Anw", "The Anw is a scheme for surviving dependants and not a scheme for incapacity for work."]], "1d.9"],
["Dennis Kuipers (34) started his own business as a carpenter three years ago. He works as a self-employed person without staff for various clients and has no employees. After a fall from scaffolding he realises he does not know what happens if he cannot work for a long time. He asks which statutory provision protects him. What is correct?", [["As a self-employed person he does not in principle fall under the WIA and must cover this risk himself", "The WIA is an employee insurance. A self-employed person can cover the risk, for example, with disability insurance or a mutual self-employed support fund (broodfonds)."], ["He automatically falls under the WIA as soon as he is registered with the Chamber of Commerce", "Registration with the Chamber of Commerce does not make him an employee; the WIA applies to employees."], ["He receives an AOW (state pension) benefit as soon as he becomes incapacitated for work", "The AOW is an old-age provision from the AOW age."], ["He is entitled to a WW (unemployment benefit) for as long as he cannot work", "The WW is an employee insurance for unemployment, not for incapacity for work."]], "1d.13"],
["Marloes (48) has become a widow; her husband died suddenly. They have two children aged 19 and 21, who still live at home. Marloes works four days a week and is healthy. She asks whether she can receive a surviving dependants' benefit under the Anw. What is correct?", [["No, because she is not caring for a child under 18 and is not incapacitated for work", "An Anw benefit is available only under strict conditions, such as caring for a child under 18 or at least 45% incapacity for work. Marloes does not meet these."], ["Yes, every surviving dependant of a deceased spouse is entitled to the Anw until AOW age", "The Anw has strict conditions; by no means every surviving dependant is entitled."], ["Yes, because she is over 45 and therefore always entitled to the Anw", "Age alone does not give entitlement; that rule applies only to surviving dependants born before 1950."], ["Yes, but only for her children, because the Anw is paid to orphans", "An orphan's benefit exists only if both parents have died; the children still have their mother."]], "1d.6"],
["How does someone build up entitlement to the AOW (state pension)?", [["2% per year of living or working in the Netherlands in the 50 years before AOW age", "Anyone who has been insured for that full period is entitled to a full AOW; each missing year costs 2%."], ["By paying premiums each year into an individual pension pot that is invested by the SVB", "The AOW is a pay-as-you-go system; no individual pot is built up."], ["Only through the employer with a pension fund", "Pension through the employer is the second pillar; the AOW is the first pillar."], ["With 1% for each year someone has worked as an employee", "The build-up depends on living or working in the Netherlands, not only on employment, and amounts to 2% per year."]], "1d.8"],
["According to the SFDR, what is the difference between an Article 8 and an Article 9 product?", [["An Article 8 product promotes environmental or social characteristics; an Article 9 product has sustainable investments as its objective", "Article 9 products have sustainability as an explicit objective and are often described as dark green."], ["An Article 8 product has sustainable investments as its objective; an Article 9 product only promotes environmental or social characteristics", "This is exactly the wrong way round."], ["An Article 8 product is always a savings product; an Article 9 product always an equity fund", "The articles concern sustainability ambition, not the type of product."], ["There is no difference; both articles apply to all investment funds", "The articles in fact distinguish products with a different sustainability profile."]], "1b.17"],
["What is a sustainability risk within the meaning of the SFDR?", [["An environmental, social or governance event or condition that could cause a material negative impact on the value of an investment", "It concerns the risk that sustainability factors affect the value of the investment."], ["The risk that a sustainable investment yields a lower return than the average market over a period of five years", "A lower return in itself is not a sustainability risk within the meaning of the SFDR."], ["The risk that a client has no sustainability preferences", "Client preferences are a different concept from the sustainability risk of an investment."], ["The risk that the AFM assesses a product as not sustainable", "The SFDR describes the risk from the perspective of the investment, not of the supervisor."]], "1b.17"],
["For which services must an adviser in principle ask about the client's sustainability preferences?", [["When advising on insurance-based investment products and for investment advice", "Since 2 August 2022, sustainability preferences have been part of the suitability assessment for these forms of advice."], ["For every non-life insurance policy, such as a car insurance policy", "This enquiry does not apply to ordinary non-life insurance."], ["Only for commercial clients with more than fifty employees that fall under the CSRD reporting obligation", "The enquiry in fact applies to advice to clients, regardless of the number of employees."], ["Never; asking about sustainability is entirely voluntary", "For the forms of advice mentioned it is a mandatory component."]], "1f.15"],
["What classification of sustainability preferences does European regulation use in advice?", [["A minimum proportion of taxonomy-aligned investments, a minimum proportion of sustainable investments (SFDR) and attention to principal adverse impacts", "A client can indicate one or more of these preferences, which the adviser takes into account in their advice."], ["A preference for a low, medium or high return", "A wish for return belongs to the client's objectives, not to sustainability preferences."], ["A preference for Dutch, European or worldwide investments", "A regional preference is not a statutory category of sustainability preferences."], ["A preference for green, orange or red according to the AFM sustainability label, supplemented by a minimum ESG score per fund", "There is no statutory AFM colour label for sustainability preferences."]], "1f.15"],
["An adviser presents an investment insurance policy as 'completely green', while the provider does not classify the product as sustainable and there is no substantiation. What is correct?", [["This is greenwashing: misleading information, contrary to the requirement that information be correct, clear and not misleading", "Sustainability claims must be accurate and substantiated, just like other product information."], ["This is permitted, because sustainability is a subjective concept", "Sustainability claims must also be factually correct and substantiated."], ["This is permitted if the client has no sustainability preferences, because sustainability then plays no role in the advice", "Information may not be misleading even towards a client without preferences."], ["This is only a problem if the AFM has approved the product in advance", "The AFM does not approve products in advance; the information obligation always applies."]], "4a.4"],
["In investment advice a client says they have no sustainability preferences. What is correct?", [["The adviser records this; they may then advise both products with and without sustainable characteristics", "A client without preferences is treated as sustainability-neutral; the advice must otherwise simply be suitable."], ["The adviser may then only advise products without any sustainable characteristic, such as an Article 6 product", "Products with sustainable characteristics may also be recommended to a client without preferences."], ["The adviser may then no longer give the client advice", "The absence of preferences is no obstacle to advice."], ["The adviser must oblige the client to choose a preference after all", "Stating preferences is the client's choice, not an obligation."]], "1f.15"],
["Ingrid saves €150.00 every month because in three years she wants to take a world trip. Which saving motive does this correspond to?", [["The goal motive", "Ingrid is saving for a specific goal at a particular time: the world trip."], ["The security motive", "With the security motive someone saves a buffer for unexpected expenses, such as a broken washing machine."], ["The wealth motive", "With the wealth motive someone saves to build up wealth, without a specific spending goal."], ["The transaction motive", "This is not one of the three saving motives; it concerns holding money for daily payments."]], "1b.6"],
["Why does a bank attract consumers' savings?", [["Because savings are a relatively cheap source of funding for the credit the bank provides", "The bank uses the savings to provide mortgages, for example. The difference between the interest received and the interest paid is an important source of income."], ["Because the bank is legally obliged to hold a savings account for every client", "There is no statutory obligation to give every client a savings account."], ["Because savings are not on the bank's balance sheet and therefore pose no risk", "Savings are a debt of the bank to the saver and are in fact on the balance sheet."], ["Because the bank never has to pay interest on savings to the saver", "The bank does pay interest; it earns from the difference with the interest on credit."]], "1b.7"],
["Baker Kees buys a new oven for his bakery so that he can bake more bread. His neighbour buys shares in a listed fund and his son puts money into a savings account. Which statement is correct?", [["Kees invests capital, the neighbour invests in securities, the son saves", "Making a capital investment means spending money on means of production such as an oven. Investing in securities means deploying wealth for a return with more risk; saving means putting money aside safely."], ["Kees invests in securities, the neighbour makes a capital investment and the son saves", "An oven for one's own business is a capital investment, not an investment in securities."], ["All three invest in securities, because they are all putting money aside for later", "Saving, investing in securities and capital investment differ in purpose and risk."], ["Kees saves, because the oven can be sold again later", "Buying a means of production is a capital investment, even if it is sold later."]], "1b.10"],
["The AFM establishes that a day-to-day policymaker of an advisory firm is no longer reliable. The firm does nothing. Which measure is, among others, available to the AFM?", [["It can ultimately withdraw the firm's licence", "Anyone who no longer meets the licensing requirements can lose their licence; withdrawal is one of the AFM's most severe measures."], ["It can impose a prison sentence on the policymaker itself", "Custodial sentences are imposed only by the criminal court, following prosecution by the Public Prosecution Service."], ["It can oblige the firm to terminate its affiliation with Kifid", "Affiliation with Kifid is in fact mandatory for providing services to consumers; terminating it is not a supervisory measure."], ["It must first await a ruling from Kifid before it may take action", "The AFM enforces independently and does not depend on a dispute procedure at Kifid."]], "1f.25"],
["What is an affiliated undertaking (aangesloten onderneming) within the meaning of the Wft?", [["An undertaking without a licence of its own that works under the responsibility of a licensed service provider", "The service provider holds a licence and vouches for the affiliated undertaking complying with the Wft rules."], ["An undertaking affiliated with Kifid that therefore no longer needs its own AFM licence for its services", "Affiliation with Kifid concerns complaint handling and does not replace the licensing requirement."], ["An undertaking that is a member of a trade organisation and therefore falls under that organisation's supervision", "A trade organisation is not a supervisor; the concept is about working under someone else's licence."], ["A subsidiary of a bank that automatically falls under DNB's prudential supervision", "That describes a group relationship, not the Wft concept of an affiliated undertaking."]], "1f.38"],
["Which insurance must an adviser or intermediary with a Wft licence in principle have?", [["Professional indemnity insurance", "It covers loss suffered by clients through professional errors; such insurance is a licensing requirement for advisers and intermediaries."], ["Legal expenses insurance for business disputes", "It may be useful for the firm, but is not a statutory licensing requirement."], ["Credit insurance for unpaid invoices from clients", "It protects the firm against non-payment, not the client against advisory errors."], ["Business interruption insurance for loss of turnover after a fire", "It covers a business risk of the firm itself and is not mandatory for the licence."]], "1f.35"],
["Esther Wouters (45) has worked as a self-employed graphic designer for ten years and builds up no pension through an employer. She has annual allowance and opens an annuity savings account at her bank. She pays €5,000.00 into it this year. She asks what the tax consequences are. What is correct?", [["Her contribution is deductible in box 1 within her annual allowance; the later payouts are taxed in box 1", "With annuity savings with a bank, the contribution is deductible within the annual or reservation allowance. In return, the payouts are taxed later in box 1; during build-up the balance does not fall in box 3."], ["Her contribution is not deductible, but the later payouts are entirely tax-free", "It is the other way round: the contribution is deductible and the payouts are taxed."], ["Her balance falls in box 3 every year and the contribution is deductible in box 2", "An annuity balance does not fall in box 3, and box 2 concerns a substantial interest."], ["She can withdraw the balance at any time without tax consequences as ordinary savings", "The balance is blocked; withdrawing earlier leads to taxation and may incur a revision interest charge."]], "1b.13"],
["What distinguishes an authorised agent from an ordinary insurance intermediary?", [["Under a power of attorney, they may conclude insurance for the insurer", "The insurer has authorised them to act on its behalf, often including premium collection and claims handling."], ["They work exclusively for individual clients and never for commercial clients", "The distinction concerns powers on behalf of the insurer, not the target group."], ["They do not need a Wft licence, because they act on behalf of the insurer", "An authorised agent also falls under the Wft and in principle needs a licence."], ["They may only advise and may never conclude an insurance policy themselves", "It is the other way round: the characteristic is that they may conclude on behalf of the insurer."]], "1g.2"],
["A firm with an AFM licence for non-life insurance also wants to start advising on mortgage credit. What must the firm do?", [["Have the licence extended to mortgage credit and ensure professional qualification", "A licence applies to the products stated in it; for a new product area an extension and appropriate professional qualification are needed."], ["Nothing, because one Wft licence automatically applies to all types of financial products", "The licence states which financial products it applies to; other products are not covered by it."], ["Only notify Kifid that the firm may now also receive mortgage complaints", "Kifid handles disputes and does not grant licences."], ["Only amend its Chamber of Commerce registration with the new activity", "A Chamber of Commerce registration is separate from the AFM licensing requirement."]], "1f.25"],
["An advisory firm wants to appoint a new director who will determine the day-to-day policy. What applies?", [["The AFM assesses their reliability and suitability, in principle in advance", "A new day-to-day policymaker must be notified to the AFM in advance and assessed."], ["The appointment only has to be mentioned in the annual report afterwards", "Afterwards is too late: the assessment in principle takes place before the policymaker starts."], ["An assessment is only needed if the director will also advise clients themselves", "The assessment relates to determining policy, not to advising oneself."], ["The Chamber of Commerce assesses whether the new director is reliable", "The Chamber of Commerce registers directors, but the assessment of reliability and suitability lies with the AFM."]], "1f.33"],
["An employee of an advisory firm only processes policy changes in the administration and has no contact with clients about financial products. Must they have a Wft diploma?", [["No, the requirements apply to work involving client contact about advice or intermediation", "Purely administrative tasks without client contact about financial products fall outside the diploma requirement."], ["Yes, every employee of a licence holder must have obtained at least Wft Basic", "The requirement depends on the activities, not on the mere fact that someone works for a licence holder."], ["Yes, because in their work they process clients' personal data and must therefore be professionally qualified under the Wft", "Processing personal data falls under the GDPR (AVG), not under the Wft professional qualification requirements."], ["Only if they have been employed by the firm for longer than a year", "The length of employment does not determine whether a diploma is needed."]], "1f.33"],
["Adviser Jasper holds the Wft Basic and Wft Non-life Insurance (Personal) diplomas. For years he has handled the insurance of the Willems family. Now the family wants to move and asks Jasper to provide mortgage advice as well. The firm does have a licence for mortgage credit. What is correct?", [["He may only do so once he is also professionally qualified for mortgage credit; until then he refers them on", "Professional qualification applies per product area. Jasper knows the limits of his expertise and puts the family in touch with a professionally qualified colleague."], ["He may advise, because Wft Basic covers the general knowledge for all product areas", "Wft Basic is not sufficient; for mortgage advice the Mortgage Credit module is also needed."], ["He may advise, because the firm has a licence for mortgage credit", "The firm's licence does not release the adviser from their own professional qualification requirements."], ["He may advise if the family declares in writing that it agrees to this", "Professional qualification requirements are statutory and cannot be set aside by the client."]], "4a.2"],
["A new employee has not yet obtained his Wft diploma but already wants to take part in advisory processes. What is possible in principle?", [["Working temporarily under the supervision of a professionally qualified colleague while he obtains his diploma", "The rules allow working under supervision for a limited period, provided a professionally qualified supervisor oversees and is responsible."], ["Advising independently, as long as the client does not know he is still in training", "Advising independently without professional qualification is not permitted, regardless of what the client knows."], ["Nothing: without a diploma he may not even be present at an advisory meeting", "Being present and taking part under supervision is possible."], ["Advising independently as soon as he has submitted an application for recognition of an old diploma as equivalent", "A submitted application is not yet recognised professional qualification."]], "1f.33"],
["The father of Jolanda and Marco has died. In his will Jolanda is appointed executor. Bills still have to be paid, such as the funeral and the last rent. Jolanda asks the bank whether a separate account can be opened to settle the estate. What is correct about an estate account (boedelrekening)?", [["It is an account in the name of the estate, which Jolanda as executor can open for the settlement", "The deceased's balances go into an estate account and the estate's debts are paid from it. It can be opened by the executor or otherwise by the heirs jointly."], ["It is an account in Jolanda's own private name, in which the inheritance immediately becomes her property", "An estate account is in the name of the estate; the money does not yet belong to an heir."], ["An estate account can only be opened by the notary, never by an heir", "The executor or the heirs jointly can also open an estate account."], ["An estate account is only needed if the heirs disclaim the estate", "An estate account serves to settle the estate, even if the heirs accept it."]], "1b.22"],
["What information must an adviser in any event obtain about the client in order to be able to advise suitably?", [["Financial position, knowledge and experience, objectives and risk appetite", "This know-your-client information forms the basis for advice that fits the client's situation."], ["Only the gross annual income and the monthly payment the client themselves wishes to pay", "That is too limited; knowledge, experience, objectives and risk appetite are also needed for suitable advice."], ["The client's preference for a particular provider and their marital status", "That may be useful, but it is not the core of the information needed for suitable advice."], ["Solely what the client volunteers, because further questioning is not permitted", "The adviser must in fact actively ask further questions to obtain a complete picture."]], "1d.1"],
["Mrs Smit (84) has been a widow for half a year. Her adviser discusses with her a proposal to place part of her savings in an investment insurance policy. During the conversation she keeps asking the same questions and does not seem to fully grasp the consequences. She says that she is fine with it if the adviser says so. What is the best course of action?", [["Take extra care, check that she genuinely understands, and where necessary involve a person she trusts", "Extra care is appropriate with a vulnerable client. The adviser must be sure that Mrs Smit understands the consequences, if necessary with the help of someone she trusts."], ["Simply complete the advice, because an adult client is responsible for their own choices", "The duty of care requires more if the client evidently does not grasp the consequences."], ["Immediately ask the AFM to assess whether Mrs Smit still has legal capacity", "The AFM does not assess individual clients for legal capacity."], ["Phone her children and complete the advice with them without her", "The client is Mrs Smit herself; without her consent you do not share data and others do not decide for her."]], "4a.1"],
["Which test must an investment firm carry out when a retail client wants to buy a complex investment product without advice?", [["An appropriateness test of the client's knowledge and experience", "Under MiFID II the firm must, for complex products without advice, check whether the client can understand the risks and warn where necessary."], ["A suitability test of financial position, objectives and risk appetite", "That more extensive test belongs to investment advice and portfolio management, not to services without advice."], ["No test at all, because the client chooses the product themselves", "An appropriateness test also applies to complex products without advice."], ["A creditworthiness assessment with a consultation of the BKR", "A creditworthiness assessment belongs to lending, not to buying investments."]], "1f.32"],
["Why does a credit provider obtain information about the consumer's financial position before granting consumer credit?", [["To prevent over-borrowing", "The creditworthiness assessment must prevent the consumer from being given credit that they cannot responsibly repay."], ["To determine the size of the intermediary's fee", "An intermediary's remuneration is separate from the purpose of the creditworthiness assessment."], ["To apply the interest rate that the AFM prescribes for this consumer", "The AFM does not prescribe interest rates per consumer."], ["To be able to share the data with other credit providers for marketing", "Use for marketing is a different purpose for which a basis of its own is needed; it is not a purpose of the assessment."]], "1c.17"],
["Gerard Hoekstra (55) has had a life insurance policy with a fixed premium since 2005. His adviser sees a comparable policy with a lower premium at another insurer. He is considering advising Gerard to surrender the old policy and take out the new one. Gerard has meanwhile developed high blood pressure. What should the adviser pay particular attention to?", [["Whether switching is favourable on balance, given surrender costs, new costs, acceptance and loss of rights", "Switching can be disadvantageous because of surrender costs, new costs and a new medical acceptance. With his high blood pressure, Gerard may moreover face a higher premium or a refusal."], ["Only whether the premium of the new policy is lower than that of his current policy", "A lower premium says nothing about the total costs, the conditions and the acceptance."], ["Whether the current insurer gives prior written permission to terminate the old policy", "That is not the point: the adviser must assess whether switching is favourable for Gerard on balance."], ["Nothing in particular, because a new policy is more modern and therefore better", "Newer is not automatically better; costs and acceptance in particular can turn out disadvantageous."]], "4a.4"],
["A client takes advice through an online advice tool, without personal contact with an adviser. What applies to the duty of care?", [["It applies in full: automated advice must also be suitable", "With automated advice too, the undertaking must obtain sufficient client information and give suitable advice."], ["It does not apply, because no human is involved in the advice", "The absence of a human adviser does not make it any less advice."], ["It applies only once the client submits a complaint afterwards", "The duty of care applies to every piece of advice in advance, not only when a complaint arrives."], ["It passes entirely to the supplier that built the advice software", "The financial undertaking remains responsible for the advice it gives through its tool."]], "1f.18"],
["An insurer has developed a product for young families with a stable income. An adviser is considering recommending it to a retired single person. What is correct?", [["They must check critically whether it fits; the client is outside the target group", "The target group from the product development process is intended for the distributor; advising outside the target group requires good justification."], ["The target group is the insurer's internal policy and plays no role for the adviser", "Distributors must in fact take the provider's target group information into account in their services."], ["They may only recommend the product if the insurer gives written permission", "The insurer's permission is not the yardstick; the question is whether the product suits the client."], ["The client must check for themselves whether they belong to the product's target group", "Safeguarding the target group is a task of the provider and the adviser, not of the client."]], "1f.15"],
["An adviser advises on mortgages using the offering of a limited number of lenders. What must they make clear to the client in advance?", [["On the basis of which offering they advise", "The client must know that the whole market is not being compared, so that they can judge the value of the advice."], ["Nothing, as long as they recommend the best product from their own selection", "Even then the client must know that the offering on which the advice is based is limited."], ["That they are independent, because they do not offer financial products themselves", "Without an analysis of a sufficient number of products on the market they may not call themselves independent."], ["That the client must approach the other lenders themselves for a comparison", "There is no such obligation for the client; the adviser must, however, be open about their offering."]], "1f.37"],
["In an advertisement for an investment product the possible return is printed large, while the risks appear only in small print at the bottom. What is correct?", [["This is misleading: advantages and risks must be presented in a balanced way", "Information, including in advertising, must be correct, clear and not misleading; risks may not be tucked away."], ["This is permitted, as long as the risks can be found somewhere in the advertisement", "Tucking risks away makes the message as a whole misleading."], ["This is only a problem if a client actually buys the product", "The standard applies to the information itself, regardless of whether a purchase follows."], ["This is allowed, because advertising does not fall under the Wft information rules", "Advertising must also meet the Wft requirements for information to clients."]], "1f.15"],
["What is the key information document (KID) under the PRIIPs Regulation?", [["A concise standard document on the features, risks and costs of packaged investment products", "The KID must enable a retail investor to understand and compare products before purchase."], ["The standardised information sheet on cover and exclusions that goes with a non-life insurance policy", "That is the insurance product information document (IPID) under the IDD."], ["The European Standardised Information Sheet that goes with a mortgage offer", "That is the ESIS under the Mortgage Credit Directive."], ["The annual statement of accrued entitlements from a pension provider", "That is the Uniform Pension Statement (Uniform Pensioenoverzicht), which has nothing to do with PRIIPs."]], "1f.2"],
["Under MiFID II, what must an investment adviser provide to a retail client before a recommended transaction is carried out?", [["A suitability statement setting out why the advice suits the client", "That statement shows how the advice matches the client's situation, objectives and preferences and makes it verifiable."], ["Only an invoice for the firm's advisory fee", "An invoice says nothing about the grounds for the advice."], ["A copy of the licence that the AFM has granted to the investment firm", "The licence status can be consulted in the public register; the point here is the grounds for the advice."], ["A written statement that the expected return is guaranteed", "Returns on investments cannot be guaranteed; such a statement would be misleading."]], "1f.32"],
["A firm wants to place mandatory pre-contractual information only on a web page that it can amend at any time. Why does that as a rule not meet the requirement of a durable medium?", [["Because the client then cannot keep the information and consult it later unchanged", "A durable medium, such as a PDF sent by email, lets the client store the information and see it again unchanged."], ["Because under the Wft pre-contractual information to clients must always be provided on paper", "Digital provision is permitted, provided it is on a durable medium such as a PDF file."], ["Because a web page only counts once the AFM has approved the text in advance", "The AFM does not approve undertakings' information in advance."], ["Because the client has to create an account to read a web page", "The problem is not access but that the content can be changed and is not kept by the client."]], "1f.3"],
["What does an overview of the cumulative costs of an investment product mainly show the client?", [["How much the costs together reduce the return", "Costs reduce the return anew every year; the overview makes this combined effect visible."], ["How much commission the adviser receives from the provider", "For investment services to individuals a commission ban applies; the overview concerns the costs to the client."], ["What returns the product has achieved in the past", "Historical return is something different from the effect of costs on the return."], ["How great the chance is that the investment falls in value", "That is risk information; the cost overview is about the influence of costs."]], "1f.3"],
["Bas buys a €1,200.00 television in an electronics shop and pays for it to the shop in instalments. He takes the set with him straight away, but receives no money. Which form of credit is this?", [["Goods credit", "With goods credit the consumer receives a good whose price they pay in instalments. No money is paid out to them."], ["Money credit", "With money credit the consumer receives a sum of money that they can spend."], ["Current account credit", "That is an overdraft on a current account up to an agreed limit."], ["Mortgage credit", "Mortgage credit is a loan with a mortgage right on registered property as security."]], "1c.4"],
["What are appropriate measures for managing conflicts of interest within an advisory firm?", [["Segregation of duties, pay policy without sales incentives, register of gifts and secondary positions", "Organisational measures like these reduce the chance that own interests influence the advice."], ["Asking employees to keep conflicts of interest to themselves so as not to unnecessarily worry or deter clients", "Concealing manages nothing; conflicts of interest must in fact be identified and addressed."], ["Having all clients sign in advance that they waive protection against conflicts of interest", "A client cannot waive statutory protection in advance; the undertaking must take measures itself."], ["Always advising the provider that brings the firm the most turnover, so that there is no doubt", "That is precisely the conflict of interest that must be prevented."]], "1f.33"],
["Does a ban on commission from providers also apply to investment advice and portfolio management for retail investors?", [["Yes, in principle no commission may be accepted from providers in that case either", "For investment services to individuals a ban comparable to the commission ban for complex products applies."], ["No, the commission ban applies exclusively to mortgage credit", "The commission ban and the ban for investment services extend further than mortgages alone."], ["No, commission is permitted as long as the adviser discloses the amount to the client in advance", "Disclosure alone is not enough; a ban applies for these services."], ["Only for portfolio management, not for investment advice", "The ban applies to both forms of investment services."]], "1f.8"],
["An intermediary in personal non-life insurance receives commission from the insurer. What must they in any event tell the client under the IDD?", [["What the nature of their remuneration is", "The client must know how the intermediary is paid, for example through commission included in the premium, in order to be able to assess the advice."], ["Nothing, because commission is permitted for non-life insurance", "Commission is allowed here, but transparency about the nature of the remuneration remains mandatory."], ["How much they earn in commission in total per year", "They do not have to disclose the intermediary's total annual income; what matters is the nature of the remuneration for this product."], ["That the client must always pay the commission separately", "With non-life insurance the commission is in fact usually included in the premium."]], "1f.7"],
["An insurer holds a substantial proportion of the shares of an advisory firm. What must the firm do in this connection?", [["Inform the client in advance about this capital relationship with the insurer", "A capital interest can influence the advice; the client must therefore be aware of it."], ["Nothing, because the firm's ownership structure is confidential business information", "It is precisely such relationships that the client needs to know in order to judge the independence of the advice."], ["From now on advise only this insurer's products to all clients", "The interest does not oblige this; it must be made transparent and managed."], ["Let the insurer decide which clients the firm does and does not accept", "That would increase the conflict of interest instead of managing it."]], "1f.36"],
["Monique Dekker has solved a complicated mortgage and insurance matter after a renovation for the Van Leeuwen couple. The couple is very satisfied. At the last meeting they give her an expensive watch as thanks. Monique finds it awkward to refuse the gift. What is the best course of action?", [["Follow the firm's gifts policy and as a rule refuse or report such a valuable gift", "A valuable gift can undermine the adviser's independence or give that appearance. The gifts policy determines what is permitted; an expensive watch is usually refused or reported."], ["Accept the watch, because gifts from clients are a private matter for the adviser", "Gifts affect the firm's integrity and fall under the gifts policy."], ["Accept the watch and give the couple a discount on the next piece of advice", "That links the gift to a reciprocal benefit and makes the conflict of interest greater."], ["Sell the watch and quietly add the proceeds to the firm's cash", "This is not transparent and does not solve the integrity problem."]], "4a.4"],
["Within what period must a consumer as a rule submit their complaint to Kifid after the financial service provider has taken a final position?", [["Within three months", "As a main rule Kifid applies a period of three months after the service provider's final position."], ["Within fourteen days", "Kifid has no such short period; fourteen days is the period of the right of withdrawal for distance contracts."], ["Within five years", "Five years is the limitation period for a claim, not the period for a complaint to Kifid."], ["No period applies", "Kifid does apply periods, so that disputes are handled in good time."]], "1f.5"],
["What does it mean if the parties at Kifid opt for binding advice?", [["Both parties are bound by the ruling; the court reviews it only to a very limited extent", "With binding advice the parties agree in advance to accept the ruling; annulment by the court is possible only in exceptional cases."], ["Only the consumer is bound; the service provider may set the ruling aside without consequences", "With binding advice both parties are in fact bound."], ["The ruling is non-binding advice that the parties may or may not follow", "That describes non-binding advice."], ["The AFM ensures enforcement of the ruling by imposing a fine", "The AFM plays no role in enforcing Kifid rulings."]], "1f.21"],
["Eva Janssen (33) buys her first apartment. She borrows €250,000.00 from a bank. At the notary she signs the mortgage deed, by which the bank obtains a mortgage right on the apartment. Eva wonders who the mortgagor is in this deed. What is correct?", [["Eva is the mortgagor and the bank is the mortgagee", "Eva grants the mortgage right on her apartment to the bank. The bank takes that right as security and is therefore the mortgagee."], ["The bank is the mortgagor, because it provides the money", "It concerns the mortgage right, not the money: Eva grants that right to the bank."], ["The notary is the mortgagor, because he draws up the deed", "The notary is not a party to the mortgage right; he records it."], ["Eva and the bank are both mortgagee", "There is one mortgagor, Eva, and one mortgagee, the bank."]], "1c.9"],
["Jesse (29) and Mila (28) have made an offer of €400,000.00 on a terraced house, and the offer has been accepted. According to the valuation report, the market value of the home is €380,000.00. They want to borrow the full purchase price. Their income is more than sufficient. What is the consequence of the lower valuation?", [["They can in principle borrow a maximum of the market value and pay the difference themselves", "The lender bases the maximum loan on the valued market value, not on the purchase price. They contribute the amount above that, plus the buyer's costs, themselves."], ["The valuation plays no role, because the bank takes the purchase price as its starting point", "The loan is in fact related to the valued market value."], ["They can borrow more, because their income is more than sufficient", "Besides income, the value of the home is also a limit for the mortgage."], ["The seller must reduce the purchase price to the valued market value", "The purchase contract remains in force; the valuation does not change the purchase price."]], "1c.15"],
["What is an important advantage of Kifid for a consumer compared with court proceedings?", [["Kifid is accessible, cheaper and expert in financial matters", "As a result a consumer can have a dispute assessed without high costs or a lawyer."], ["Kifid can have the service provider convicted in criminal proceedings", "Kifid is a dispute resolution body and has no criminal-law powers."], ["A Kifid ruling is always binding on both parties", "Whether a ruling is binding depends on the parties' choice."], ["At Kifid the complaint does not first have to be submitted to the service provider", "For Kifid too, the consumer must first put their complaint to the service provider."]], "1f.5"],
["What are the three classic stages of money laundering?", [["Placement, layering and integration", "Criminal money is brought into the financial system, its origin is concealed and the money apparently returns legally into the economy."], ["Identification, verification and reporting", "These are steps an institution takes in customer due diligence and reporting, not stages of money laundering."], ["Acquisition, spending and investment", "These are not recognised stages of the money laundering process."], ["Receipt, transfer and repayment", "This describes payment transactions, not the stages in which money is laundered."]], "4a.3"],
["What does the risk-based approach under the Wwft entail?", [["The intensity of customer due diligence is tailored to the risk", "The risk of the customer, product, transaction and country determines how in-depth the investigation must be."], ["Only clients with a high income need to be investigated", "Income is not the yardstick; what matters is the risk of money laundering or terrorist financing."], ["All clients receive exactly the same investigation, regardless of their profile", "The Wwft in fact requires customisation by risk: lighter where possible, heavier where necessary."], ["The client decides for themselves which risk profile suits them", "The institution makes the risk assessment itself."]], "2b.1"],
["A regular client with a simple, low risk profile comes in for a new product. When may an institution make do with simplified customer due diligence?", [["If its risk assessment shows that the risk of money laundering is demonstrably low", "Simplified due diligence is permitted only on the basis of a substantiated risk assessment; ongoing monitoring remains necessary."], ["Always, as soon as someone has been a client for more than a year and has never caused problems", "The length of the relationship does not determine the risk."], ["If the client declares in writing that their money was earned legally", "The client's own declaration does not replace a risk assessment."], ["If the adviser is busy and catches up on the due diligence later", "Workload is no ground for limiting the due diligence."]], "2b.1"],
["According to the Wwft, when is there a subjective indicator of an unusual transaction?", [["If the institution has reason to suspect that the transaction is connected with money laundering or terrorist financing", "With a subjective indicator, the institution's judgement on the basis of the circumstances is decisive."], ["If the transaction exceeds an amount laid down by regulation, regardless of all further circumstances of the case", "That is an objective indicator: the report then follows from a fixed criterion."], ["If the adviser personally does not like the client and therefore doubts their story", "Personal feelings are not a ground; what matters is indications of money laundering or terrorist financing."], ["If the AFM has designated the transaction as suspicious in advance", "The AFM does not assess transactions in advance; the institution assesses for itself."]], "3b.2"],
["An intermediary notices that a client's transaction is unusual. When must they report it to FIU-Nederland?", [["Without delay after the unusual nature has become known", "The Wwft requires a prompt report, so that FIU-Nederland can analyse it in good time."], ["Within a year after the end of the financial year in which the transaction took place", "Such a long period would make the reporting obligation pointless."], ["Only once it is established that it really is money laundering", "Certainty is not needed; an unusual transaction is reported, and FIU does the analysis."], ["Only if the client agrees to the report", "Agreement is not needed; the client may not even be informed of the report."]], "3b.2"],
["Who supervises compliance with the Wwft by an intermediary in life insurance?", [["The AFM", "For financial service providers such as intermediaries in life insurance, the AFM is the Wwft supervisor."], ["FIU-Nederland", "FIU-Nederland receives and analyses reports, but does not supervise compliance."], ["The Public Prosecution Service", "The Public Prosecution Service prosecutes criminal offences, but is not a Wwft supervisor."], ["The Tax and Customs Administration", "The Tax and Customs Administration exercises Wwft supervision over other groups, such as certain traders, not over financial intermediaries."]], "1f.20"],
["Who is as a rule a UBO (ultimate beneficial owner) of a BV (private limited company)?", [["A natural person who holds more than 25% of the shares or voting rights, or otherwise has actual control", "The UBO is the human being behind the legal entity who ultimately owns or controls it."], ["Every statutory director of the BV, regardless of whether they hold shares or have control in some other way", "A director counts only as a pseudo-UBO when no real UBO can be established."], ["The bank where the BV holds its business account and where the assets are held", "A bank that manages an account is not an owner or holder of control."], ["Every employee of the BV who participates in a share option scheme", "Participation in an option scheme does not automatically give more than a 25% interest or control."]], "1b.3"],
["Bas Verhoef (42) comes to the office for a life insurance policy with a single premium. When you ask for his proof of identity, he shows his bank card and a passport that expired a year ago. According to him his new passport is not ready yet. In his wallet he also has a valid Dutch driving licence. What is correct?", [["The bank card and the expired passport are insufficient; his valid driving licence can be used", "For identification a valid document is needed, such as a passport, identity card or Dutch driving licence. A bank card and an expired passport do not meet that."], ["The expired passport is sufficient, because the personal details have not changed", "An expired document is not a valid proof of identity."], ["The bank card is sufficient, because the bank has already identified Bas", "A bank card is not an identity document; the firm must identify for itself."], ["Identification is only needed if Bas wants to pay the single premium in cash", "Customer due diligence is needed when entering into the relationship, regardless of the method of payment."]], "1a.9"],
["What does the Sanctions Act essentially mean for a financial undertaking?", [["It may not provide funds or services to persons and organisations on sanctions lists", "That is why the undertaking checks its clients against sanctions lists and freezes balances where necessary."], ["It must report every client with a payment arrear to the AFM", "Payment arrears have nothing to do with the Sanctions Act."], ["It must report unusual transactions to Kifid", "Unusual transactions are reported to FIU-Nederland under the Wwft; Kifid handles disputes."], ["It may itself impose financial sanctions on clients who repeatedly fail to pay their premium on time", "The Sanctions Act is about international sanctions measures, not about sanctions against clients."]], "4a.3"],
["Frank Mol, as a new client, wants to pay a single premium of €40,000.00 for an annuity insurance policy. He wants to hand over most of it in cash at the office. When asked where the money comes from, he says only that it was saved. By his own account he has a modest income. What must the intermediary subject to the Wwft do?", [["Ask further about the origin and report the transaction to FIU-Nederland if it remains unusual", "A large cash payment without a plausible origin is a strong signal. If the transaction remains unusual, the intermediary reports it to FIU-Nederland."], ["Carry out the transaction, because cash is legal tender", "That cash is legal tender does not remove the duty to report unusual transactions."], ["Warn Frank that he will be reported, so that he can prepare an explanation", "It is prohibited to let the client know that a report is being made."], ["Refer Frank to another intermediary and do nothing further", "Referring on does not release the intermediary from their reporting duty."]], "3b.2"],
["Who supervises compliance with the GDPR (AVG) in the Netherlands?", [["The Dutch Data Protection Authority", "The Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens (AP) is the Dutch privacy supervisor and can, among other things, impose fines."], ["The Netherlands Authority for the Financial Markets (AFM)", "The AFM supervises conduct on the financial markets, not privacy rules."], ["The Authority for Consumers and Markets (ACM)", "The ACM supervises competition and general consumer law, not the GDPR (AVG)."], ["Kifid (Dutch Financial Services Complaints Institute)", "Kifid settles financial disputes and is not a supervisor."]], "1f.39"],
["For every quotation request for a car insurance policy, an advisory firm also asks about the client's religion and medical history. Which GDPR (AVG) principle is mainly being infringed here?", [["Data minimisation", "No more personal data may be processed than is necessary for the purpose; this data is not needed for car insurance."], ["Accuracy", "The problem is not that the data is incorrect, but that it is not necessary."], ["Right to data portability", "That is a right of the data subject to take data with them, not a principle that is infringed here."], ["Integrity and confidentiality", "That principle is about security; here the issue is the collection of excessive data."]], "1f.40"],
["How long may an advisory firm retain clients' personal data under the GDPR (AVG)?", [["No longer than necessary for the purpose, unless the law requires retention", "The GDPR (AVG) has no fixed period; the undertaking determines it on the basis of purpose and statutory obligations."], ["Indefinitely, as long as the data is well protected against break-ins and loss", "Good security does not justify retaining data for longer than necessary."], ["Always exactly seven years, for all types of personal data and regardless of the purpose", "The seven-year tax retention obligation applies to the records, not as a general GDPR (AVG) period."], ["At most one month after the advice is completed", "No such fixed short period exists and it would clash with statutory retention obligations."]], "4a.5"],
["What conditions must consent meet under the GDPR (AVG) in order to be valid?", [["Free, specific, informed and unambiguous, and always withdrawable", "Only then can consent serve as the basis for processing."], ["Given orally to an employee and not withdrawable afterwards", "Consent must be demonstrable and can always be withdrawn."], ["Inferred from the fact that the client did not untick a pre-ticked box", "Pre-ticked boxes do not produce unambiguous consent."], ["Made a condition of every service, even if the data is not needed", "Forcing consent for non-essential data is not freely given."]], "1f.40"],
["A former client asks the firm to delete all his data. His client relationship ended two years ago; at the time the firm carried out customer due diligence under the Wwft. What is correct?", [["The firm deletes what is no longer needed, but keeps what the law requires it to retain", "The right to erasure gives way to a statutory retention obligation, such as the Wwft period of five years after the end of the relationship."], ["The firm must delete everything immediately, including the data from the customer due diligence", "Data for which a statutory retention obligation applies may not be destroyed earlier."], ["The firm may ignore the request, because a former client no longer has GDPR (AVG) rights", "Former clients are also data subjects with rights under the GDPR (AVG)."], ["The firm must first ask the AFM for permission before it may delete a former client's data", "No permission from the AFM is needed to handle an erasure request."]], "1f.39"],
["What is meant by the housing cost ratio (woonquote)?", [["The part of income that a household spends on housing costs", "The housing cost ratio expresses housing costs, such as rent or mortgage payments, as a percentage of income."], ["The ratio between the mortgage and the market value of the home", "That is the loan-to-value ratio, not the housing cost ratio."], ["The number of years needed to repay a mortgage in full", "That is the term of the loan."], ["The percentage of the WOZ value (property valuation) that is added to income", "That resembles the notional rental value (eigenwoningforfait), which has nothing to do with the housing cost ratio."]], "1c.19"],
["Mark (31) and Sophie (29) are buying a home below the cost limit of the NHG (National Mortgage Guarantee). Their adviser recommends taking out the mortgage with NHG. Mark asks what NHG exactly does for them. Sophie asks why the bank then charges a lower interest rate. What is the essence of NHG?", [["A guarantee for the loan; in the event of a forced sale through no fault of their own, a residual debt can be waived", "With NHG the lender runs less risk and therefore often gives an interest rate discount. If Mark and Sophie have to sell the home at a loss through no fault of their own, the residual debt can be waived."], ["The government takes over their monthly payments for as long as one of them is unemployed or incapacitated for work", "NHG does not take over monthly payments; help with payment problems may, however, be available."], ["They always get a mortgage, even if their income is actually insufficient for the loan", "Even with NHG the normal lending standards for income and home value apply."], ["The home is thereby insured against fire and storm damage", "That is arranged by a buildings insurance policy, not by NHG."]], "1c.20"],
["What is the role of the notary in buying a home with a mortgage?", [["They draw up the transfer deed and mortgage deed, have them registered in the Land Registry (Kadaster) and settle the payments", "The notary ensures that ownership passes validly and that the mortgage right comes into being through registration in the public registers. The money goes through their third-party funds account."], ["They advise the buyer which mortgage and which lender suit them best", "Mortgage advice is the task of an adviser; the notary is impartial."], ["They value the home and establish the market value for the lender", "That is done by a valuer, not the notary."], ["They assess on behalf of the lender whether the buyer can bear the monthly payments on the loan", "The lender assesses creditworthiness itself."]], "1c.21"],
["Iris (40) and Bart (42) are taking out a new mortgage. They can choose between a fixed-rate period of 5, 10 or 20 years. Iris wants certainty about the monthly payments for as long as possible. Bart wants the lowest possible interest rate. What is as a rule correct, assuming a normal interest rate structure?", [["A longer fixed-rate period gives more certainty, but usually has a higher interest rate", "With a normal interest rate structure the lender charges a higher rate for a longer fixed-rate period, because it bears the interest rate risk for longer."], ["A longer fixed-rate period gives more certainty and also always has the lowest interest rate", "With a normal interest rate structure the rate for a longer period is in fact higher."], ["The length of the fixed-rate period has no influence on the level of the interest rate", "The interest rate in fact differs by fixed-rate period."], ["A shorter fixed-rate period gives more certainty, because the interest rate is adjusted more often", "Adjusting more often in fact means less certainty about future monthly payments."]], "1c.26"],
["Peter Groen (56) receives, via his intermediary, the annual statement for his home insurance. The statement shows the premium, policy costs and insurance premium tax. He asks why he pays tax on an insurance policy and what it is calculated on. He thinks it is VAT. What is correct?", [["It is insurance premium tax on the non-life insurance, calculated on the premium including the costs", "Insurance premium tax is payable on the premium of most non-life insurance policies. It is calculated on premium and costs together; VAT is not levied on the premium."], ["It is VAT, which is calculated on all the intermediary's services", "No VAT is levied on insurance premiums, but insurance premium tax."], ["Insurance premium tax is calculated only on the policy costs, not on the premium", "The tax is calculated on the premium and the costs together."], ["Insurance premium tax is a voluntary contribution that he may refuse", "It is a statutory tax that the insurer collects and remits."]], "1d.11"],
["What falls under the Wft standard of sound and ethical business operations?", [["Preventing conflicts of interest, criminal offences and conduct that damages trust", "Sound and ethical business operations protect trust in the undertaking and in the financial markets."], ["Only the timely filing of the annual accounts and the directors' report with the Chamber of Commerce", "That is a company-law obligation, not an elaboration of the integrity standard."], ["Maximising profit for the shareholders", "Profit maximisation is not an integrity standard and may even clash with it."], ["Solely compliance with the privacy rules of the GDPR (AVG)", "Privacy is one component; the integrity standard is much broader."]], "1f.33"],
["What is the purpose of an internal reporting scheme for suspected wrongdoing, also known as a whistleblower scheme?", [["Employees can safely report wrongdoing without being disadvantaged", "This brings wrongdoing to light sooner and protects reporters."], ["Clients can submit a complaint about the quality of the firm's services", "The internal complaints procedure serves that purpose."], ["The employer can monitor employees' private use of the internet", "A reporting scheme is not a monitoring tool for the employer."], ["Employees report clients' unusual transactions to FIU-Nederland", "That is the reporting obligation under the Wwft, something different from a whistleblower scheme."]], "4a.3"],
["At an advisory firm the bookkeeper discovers that employee Erwin has had clients' premiums transferred to his own account. It concerns dozens of clients and well over €25,000.00. The owner wants to prevent reputational damage. He is considering keeping the matter quiet and simply dismissing Erwin. What must the firm in any event do?", [["Prevent further harm, help the victims and report the incident to the AFM", "Fraud by an employee is an incident that the financial undertaking reports to the supervisor. In addition the clients must be helped, for example by restoring their cover."], ["Handle the matter internally to prevent reputational damage to the firm", "Keeping it quiet leaves the victims out in the cold and breaches the reporting obligation."], ["Make do with dismissing Erwin, because the problem is then solved", "Dismissal does not restore the clients' loss and does not replace the report."], ["Wait to see whether the prejudiced clients submit a complaint to Kifid", "The firm must take action itself; the clients may not even know that they have been prejudiced."]], "4a.3"],
["Which statutory scheme pays for long-term care, such as a stay in a nursing home because of dementia?", [["The Long-term Care Act (Wlz)", "The Wlz is a national insurance for people who permanently need care or supervision 24 hours a day."], ["The Health Insurance Act (Zvw)", "The Zvw covers basic care, such as the GP and the hospital, but not a long-term stay in a nursing home."], ["The Social Support Act (Wmo)", "The Wmo arranges support at home by the municipality, not a long-term stay in an institution."], ["A supplementary health insurance policy", "A supplementary insurance policy is voluntary and does not cover a long-term stay in a nursing home."]], "1d.15"],
["Why does a financial undertaking screen employees in integrity-sensitive positions for reliability?", [["To limit integrity risks such as fraud and misuse of client data", "Reliable employees are a precondition for sound and ethical business operations."], ["To set the employee's salary on that basis", "Screening is about reliability, not remuneration."], ["Because good screening replaces the professional qualification requirements", "Reliability and professional qualification are separate requirements."], ["To be able to report the employee to FIU-Nederland if there are doubts about their background", "FIU reports concern unusual transactions, not job applicants."]], "1f.33"],
["What is the difference between the nominal and the real interest rate?", [["The real interest rate is the nominal interest rate adjusted for inflation", "The real interest rate shows how much the purchasing power of the wealth actually grows."], ["The nominal interest rate is the rate after tax, the real interest rate the one before tax", "The difference concerns inflation, not taxation."], ["The real interest rate is the rate the bank charges including arrangement costs", "Including costs gives an effective cost percentage, not a real interest rate."], ["There is no difference; they are two names for the same concept", "The concepts in fact differ through the correction for inflation."]], "1b.15"],
["A loan carries interest of 1% per month. The interest is calculated each month on the outstanding debt including interest credited. What is correct about the effective annual interest rate?", [["It is higher than 12%", "Because interest is also charged on credited interest, the effective annual interest rate is approximately 12.68% (1.01 to the power of 12, minus 1)."], ["It is exactly equal to 12%", "12% is the sum of twelve monthly rates; the interest-on-interest effect is then disregarded."], ["It is lower than 12%", "Interest on interest makes the annual rate higher, not lower."], ["It is simply 1%", "1% is the monthly rate; over a whole year the interest is much higher."]], "2a.1"],
["What is the difference between a share and a bond?", [["A shareholder is a co-owner, a bondholder is a creditor", "The bondholder is entitled to interest and repayment; the shareholder shares in profit and risk."], ["A bondholder is a co-owner; a shareholder is a creditor of the company", "This is exactly the wrong way round."], ["A share always pays a fixed annual interest, a bond never", "A fixed interest rate is characteristic of the bond; dividend on shares is not certain."], ["Both give voting rights at the general meeting of shareholders", "Voting rights belong to shares, not to bonds."]], "1b.17"],
["What usually happens to the price of existing fixed-rate bonds when the market interest rate rises?", [["The price falls", "New bonds then offer more interest, so existing bonds with a lower interest rate become worth less."], ["The price rises", "A rising market interest rate in fact makes existing bonds with a lower interest rate less attractive."], ["The price stays the same, because the interest rate is fixed", "The fixed coupon rate does not change, but the market value of the bond does."], ["The bond is automatically redeemed early", "A change in interest rates does not automatically lead to early redemption."]], "1b.19"],
["Which risk can an investor mainly reduce by diversifying across many different investments?", [["The specific risk of individual companies", "Setbacks at one company weigh less heavily if the wealth is spread across many investments."], ["The market risk of the stock market as a whole, for example in a crisis", "Diversification within the same market does not remove market risk; if the whole market falls, the portfolio falls with it."], ["Inflation risk, which thereby disappears completely", "Diversification does not fully protect against loss of value through inflation."], ["Every risk, so that loss becomes impossible", "Diversification reduces risks, but never rules out loss."]], "1b.18"],
["Ruud works in construction and is obliged to participate in the pension fund of his industry. His wife works at a large chemical group with its own pension fund. Which description fits Ruud's pension fund?", [["An industry-wide pension fund, in which participation may have been made mandatory for the whole industry", "A bpf (industry-wide pension fund) carries out the pension scheme for an entire industry. The government can make participation mandatory for all employers in that sector."], ["A company pension fund, which works for one company or group", "That fits his wife's fund, not a fund for the whole construction sector."], ["A general pension fund, which is intended only for the self-employed", "An apf (general pension fund) carries out schemes for several unconnected employers, not only for the self-employed."], ["A premium pension institution, which only manages and pays out annuities of individual savers", "A ppi (premium pension institution) carries out defined-contribution schemes for employers, not annuities of individuals."]], "1d.19"],
["Someone will receive €1,100.00 in exactly one year. The discount rate is 10% per year. What is the present value of that amount today?", [["€1,000.00", "Present value = 1,100 divided by 1.10 = €1,000.00."], ["€990.00", "Here 10% of €1,100.00 has been wrongly deducted; discounting means dividing by 1.10."], ["€1,100.00", "Money that is only received later is worth less today."], ["€1,210.00", "That is a future value after two years of interest on €1,000.00, not a present value."]], "2a.1"],
["What does the law of large numbers mean for an insurer?", [["The more similar risks it insures, the better it can predict the total amount of claims", "With a large number of similar risks the actual claims burden comes closer to the expected claims burden. As a result the insurer can calculate an appropriate premium."], ["The more clients it has, the higher the premium per client must be", "More similar risks in fact make the claims burden more predictable, not more expensive per client."], ["An insurer must by law have a minimum number of clients in order to obtain a licence", "The law of large numbers is a statistical principle, not a licensing requirement."], ["With a large number of insureds the individual claims become smaller and smaller", "The size of individual claims does not change; only the predictability of the total increases."]], "1e.1"],
["Hans Mulder (60) invests €20,000.00 in American shares quoted in dollars. After a year the share prices in dollars are exactly at the same level as at purchase. In that period the dollar has, however, fallen considerably against the euro. Hans thinks his investment has not changed in value. What is correct?", [["The value of his investment in euros has fallen", "Hans gets fewer euros back for his dollars. That is the currency risk of investing in another currency."], ["Nothing has changed, because the share prices have remained the same", "Not in dollars, but Hans counts in euros and the dollar has become worth less."], ["The value of his investment in euros has risen", "A falling dollar in fact lowers the value in euros."], ["There is only a consequence if Hans is liable to tax in the US", "Currency risk is independent of his tax liability."]], "1c.13"],
["What is the effect of investing with borrowed money?", [["Both gains and losses are magnified relative to the own contribution", "This leverage effect can make one's own capital grow quickly, but also disappear quickly."], ["Only any gains are magnified; losses stay the same", "Leverage works in both directions."], ["The risk falls, because a larger amount is invested", "Investing more with borrowed money in fact increases the risk."], ["There is no risk, because the interest on the loan is always deductible", "The interest is not always deductible and the loan has to be repaid in any case."]], "1b.18"],
["What does the investor compensation scheme protect?", [["Investors from whom a bankrupt investment firm cannot return money or securities", "In that situation the scheme pays compensation up to a maximum amount."], ["Investors against price falls of the shares and bonds in their investment portfolio", "Price losses are a normal investment risk and are not compensated."], ["Savers up to €100,000.00 per person per bank when their bank goes bankrupt", "That is the deposit guarantee scheme."], ["Investors against the consequences of their own wrong investment choices", "Own choices remain at the investor's own expense."]], "1b.21"],
["What is the difference between a sum-assured insurance and a non-life insurance policy?", [["A sum-assured insurance pays out an agreed amount; a non-life insurance policy compensates the actual loss", "With a sum-assured insurance, such as a term life insurance policy, the size of the loss plays no role."], ["A non-life insurance policy pays out an agreed amount; a sum-assured insurance compensates the actual loss", "This is exactly the wrong way round."], ["A sum-assured insurance can only be taken out by businesses, a non-life insurance policy only by individuals", "Both types are open to individuals and businesses."], ["There is no difference; the indemnity principle applies to both without exception", "The indemnity principle applies to non-life insurance, not to sum-assured insurance."]], "1g.10"],
["For what kind of risk is taking out insurance most obvious?", [["A risk with a small chance but with major financial consequences", "Someone usually cannot bear such a risk themselves; insurance spreads it across many insureds."], ["A risk with a high chance and a small loss, such as a broken umbrella", "Someone can usually better bear small losses themselves; insurance is then relatively expensive."], ["A risk that is almost certain to occur, such as normal wear and tear", "A certain event is not an uncertain risk and is therefore not insurable."], ["Any conceivable risk, regardless of the chance and the size", "Insuring is not always worthwhile; chance and size determine whether it pays off."]], "1d.2"],
["What is the difference between gross and net return on an investment?", [["Net return is the return after deduction of costs and any tax", "For the investor, what ultimately counts is what remains after costs and tax."], ["Net return is the return before deduction of costs", "That is in fact the gross return."], ["Net return is the return after correction for exchange rate differences only", "Exchange rates influence the return, but do not determine the difference between gross and net."], ["With investment funds there is no difference between gross and net", "Investment funds also charge costs that reduce the return."]], "1b.15"],
["Joris (19) borrows his father's car to drive to a party. On the way he hits a cyclist, who is injured and has a broken bicycle. The father has third-party liability insurance for the car. The cyclist asks how she can get her loss compensated. What is correct under the WAM (Motor Vehicles Liability Insurance Act)?", [["The cyclist can claim her loss directly from the car's third-party liability insurer", "The WAM makes it compulsory to insure liability for motor vehicles, in order to protect victims. An injured party has a right of their own against the insurer, even if someone other than the policyholder was driving."], ["The cyclist must report her loss to her own home contents insurance", "A home contents insurance policy does not cover this loss; the car's third-party liability insurance is intended for victims' losses."], ["The third-party liability insurance does not pay out, because Joris is not the policyholder himself", "The third-party liability cover also applies to another driver, such as Joris; the victim must be protected."], ["The cyclist can only hold Joris personally liable, who must pay the loss himself", "Precisely in order to protect victims, the WAM gives them a right against the insurer."]], "1e.10"],
["A firm did not hand over its general terms and conditions to a consumer before or at the conclusion of the contract. The client wants to annul a term. What is correct in principle?", [["The client can annul the term, as they had no reasonable opportunity to read the conditions", "Anyone who uses general terms and conditions must give the other party a reasonable opportunity to read them; otherwise terms are voidable."], ["The client can do nothing, because the conditions were once deposited with the Chamber of Commerce", "Depositing alone is as a rule insufficient if the conditions could reasonably have been handed over."], ["The client can do nothing, because in the quotation they declared with a signature that the conditions apply", "A reference or declaration of agreement does not replace the duty to make the conditions available."], ["Only the AFM can have the general terms and conditions annulled on the client's behalf", "Annulment is a right of the other party themselves; the AFM plays no role in it."]], "1g.1"],
["A consumer has a non-life insurance policy that was tacitly renewed after the first contract year. They want to switch. What applies in principle?", [["They can cancel the insurance at any time with a notice period of at most one month", "After a tacit renewal a consumer may cancel an insurance policy during the term with a short notice period."], ["They must wait until the end of the new insurance year before the policy can end", "After tacit renewal a consumer is not bound to an entire new year."], ["They can only cancel during the term if the insurer changes the premium or conditions", "A premium change gives an additional right to cancel, but cancelling is also possible without a change."], ["They cannot cancel the insurance, because they chose tacit renewal themselves", "The law in fact protects consumers against long-term commitment through tacit renewal."]], "1g.21"],
["When can a contract be annulled on the ground of mistake?", [["If concluded under a false impression, for example through incorrect information", "Mistake is a ground for annulment if the mistaken party, with a correct impression, would not have concluded the contract in that way."], ["If one of the parties regrets afterwards the arrangements it made on concluding the contract", "Regret is not a statutory ground for annulment."], ["If the price of the product bought falls sharply shortly after the contract is concluded", "Later market developments fall outside the mistake rules."], ["If the contract was concluded only orally and is not on paper", "An oral contract is as a rule simply valid."]], "1g.1"],
["The De Jong family has a dispute with the neighbours over a fence on the property boundary. In addition, daughter Lisa (17) has a dispute with an online shop over a broken laptop. The family wants help from a lawyer and, if necessary, from a barrister. They ask which insurance helps them to enforce their rights. Which insurance best fits this need?", [["Family legal expenses insurance", "This insurance provides legal help in disputes of the insured as private individuals, for example with neighbours or an online shop. How far the cover goes is stated in the conditions."], ["Personal liability insurance", "That compensates loss that the family causes to others, but does not help in enforcing their own rights."], ["Motor vehicle legal expenses insurance", "That only covers disputes connected with a motor vehicle or traffic."], ["Business legal expenses insurance", "That is intended for disputes of a business, not of a private household."]], "1e.11"],
["Willem Dijkstra (47) is married to Saskia. His best friend Paul wants to take out a €15,000.00 loan to buy a camper van. The bank wants Willem to stand personal surety for that loan. Willem wants to do so without involving Saskia. What applies in principle?", [["He needs Saskia's consent; without that consent she can annul the suretyship", "A personal suretyship requires the consent of the spouse. If it is missing, Saskia can annul the suretyship."], ["Consent is not needed, because each spouse may perform legal acts independently", "For suretyship the law in fact makes an exception: the spouse's consent is needed for it."], ["Consent is only needed if Willem and Saskia are married in community of property", "The consent requirement applies regardless of the matrimonial property regime."], ["Only Paul's bank has to approve the suretyship in advance", "The bank assesses the surety, but that does not replace the spouse's consent."]], "1a.7"],
["A client discovers an error in the performance of an assignment, but waits two years before complaining about it. What can the contractor in principle raise against them?", [["That the client did not protest within a reasonable time after discovery, so may lose their rights", "Under the duty to complain, the creditor must complain within a reasonable time after discovering the defect."], ["That by law every complaint must be submitted in writing within fourteen days of completion of the assignment", "A fixed period of fourteen days does not apply; the yardstick is 'within a reasonable time'."], ["That a complaint may only be taken up after five years", "Five years is a limitation period, not a waiting period for complaints."], ["Nothing, because a client can complain at any time without consequences", "The law does contain a duty to complain with possible loss of rights."]], "1f.5"],
["Jacco (35) has been under guardianship (curatele) for a few years because of an addiction. His sister has been appointed guardian by the subdistrict court judge. Jacco comes to the office himself and wants to take out a life insurance policy in order to leave something behind later. He would like to sign straight away. What is correct?", [["He lacks legal capacity; without the guardian's cooperation the contract is voidable", "Someone under guardianship cannot in principle perform legal acts independently. The adviser must involve the guardian, his sister."], ["He has full legal capacity, because guardianship only concerns medical decisions", "Guardianship in fact restricts legal capacity for legal acts."], ["Guardianship only has consequences for spending above a statutory threshold", "Guardianship does not work with a threshold; the guardian's cooperation is needed for this insurance too."], ["The adviser can act as guardian themselves and sign on Jacco's behalf", "The guardian is appointed by the subdistrict court judge; here that is his sister."]], "1a.11"],
["What is the difference between a national insurance and an employee insurance?", [["National insurance covers all residents in principle, employee insurance only employees", "Examples are the AOW and Anw as national insurance and the WW and WIA as employee insurance."], ["For an employee insurance all residents are insured, for a national insurance only employees", "This is exactly the wrong way round."], ["A national insurance is always voluntary, an employee insurance always compulsory", "National insurance schemes are also compulsory for those covered by them."], ["There is no difference; the two terms are used interchangeably", "The difference lies in the circle of insured persons."]], "1e.6"],
["Sevda Arslan (39) has a permanent contract as an administrative employee. She has burn-out and expects not to be able to work for a longer time. Her partner is afraid that the family will immediately lose a large part of her income. Together they ask you who will pay her income in the coming period. What is correct?", [["Her employer, which continues to pay the salary for at most 104 weeks at at least 70%", "The obligation to continue paying salary during illness lies with the employer; only after that can the WIA come into play."], ["UWV through a benefit under the Sickness Benefits Act (Ziektewet)", "The Ziektewet is a safety net for sick employees without an employer who continues to pay salary; Sevda has a permanent contract."], ["The Social Insurance Bank (SVB) through a temporary sickness benefit", "The SVB carries out national insurance schemes, such as the AOW, and does not pay salary during illness."], ["The municipality through a supplementary benefit under the Participation Act for the duration of the illness", "Social assistance is a safety net at minimum level, not the scheme for salary during illness."]], "1d.9"],
["Lars (27) worked for half a year as an employee at an online shop. Before that he travelled for a year and did not work. His temporary contract is not renewed and he applies for a WW (unemployment) benefit. He wants to know whether he is entitled to one. Which weeks requirement must he as a rule meet?", [["He must have worked as an employee for at least 26 weeks in the 36 weeks before his unemployment", "This is the weeks requirement of the WW. With half a year of work immediately before his unemployment, Lars can meet it."], ["He must have worked for at least 52 weeks with one employer in the 104 weeks before his unemployment", "No such requirement exists; the weeks requirement is about 26 of the 36 weeks, regardless of the number of employers."], ["He must have worked sufficiently in four of the five calendar years before his unemployment", "That is the years requirement, which determines whether the benefit lasts longer than the basic duration."], ["He must have been employed by the same employer for at least one full year", "The WW sets no requirement of a full year with one employer."]], "1d.7"],
["What as a rule determines how long someone is entitled to a WW (unemployment) benefit?", [["Employment history, up to a statutory maximum", "The longer someone has worked, the longer the benefit lasts, up to the maximum duration."], ["Only their age at the time of dismissal", "Age does not play a direct role; the employment history is decisive."], ["The amount of their last-earned salary", "Salary helps determine the amount, not the duration of the benefit."], ["The number of children living at home with them", "Household composition has no influence on the duration of the WW."]], "1d.9"],
["Chantal (23) works through a temping agency at a distribution centre. After a cycling accident she falls ill. Her temp contract ends during her illness, because the assignment ends. She then no longer has an employer who continues to pay her salary. Which scheme as a rule forms her safety net?", [["The Sickness Benefits Act (Ziektewet)", "The Ziektewet is the safety net for sick employees without an employer who continues to pay salary, such as temp workers whose contract ends."], ["The AOW (state pension)", "The AOW is an old-age pension from the AOW age."], ["The Anw (Surviving Dependants Act)", "The Anw is a provision for surviving dependants."], ["The Act on Incapacity for Work Provision for Young Disabled Persons (Wajong)", "The Wajong is for people who became incapacitated for work at a young age, not for temporary illness."]], "1d.7"],
["What characterises social assistance under the Participation Act?", [["A safety net at social minimum level, run by the municipality, with an income and asset test", "Social assistance is intended for those who have insufficient means of their own and cannot rely on other provisions."], ["A UWV benefit without any test on income or assets", "Social assistance is provided by the municipality and in fact has a means test."], ["An employee insurance for which employees pay premiums and build up rights during their working lives", "Social assistance is paid from general funds and is not an employee insurance."], ["A supplement that anyone can receive on top of a high income", "Social assistance is only for those who are at risk of falling below the social minimum."]], "1e.6"],
["Which body carries out the AOW, the Anw and child benefit?", [["The Social Insurance Bank (SVB)", "The SVB carries out the national insurance schemes and child benefit."], ["The Employee Insurance Agency (UWV)", "UWV carries out the employee insurance schemes, such as the WW and the WIA."], ["The Benefits Service (Dienst Toeslagen)", "The Benefits Service pays out allowances, such as healthcare allowance and rent allowance."], ["The municipality", "The municipality carries out, among other things, the Participation Act."]], "1d.8"],
["How is the AOW age determined?", [["It is linked to life expectancy and is set a few years in advance", "That way people know in good time when their AOW starts."], ["It is fixed for everyone at 65 years", "The AOW age of 65 has been abandoned; it moves with life expectancy."], ["Everyone chooses their own AOW age", "The AOW age is set by law and cannot be chosen oneself."], ["It depends on the number of years someone has lived or worked in the Netherlands", "The number of years of residence or work determines the size of the AOW, not the starting age."]], "1d.8"],
["What is the EU taxonomy?", [["A European classification system for environmentally sustainable economic activities", "The taxonomy lays down when an activity makes a substantial contribution to environmental objectives without significantly harming other objectives."], ["A European tax on the CO2 emissions of companies and investment funds", "The taxonomy is not a tax but a classification system."], ["A quality mark that the AFM awards to financial products that are demonstrably sustainable", "The AFM does not award a sustainability quality mark; the taxonomy is European regulation."], ["A list of investments that are prohibited for consumers", "The taxonomy prohibits nothing; it describes what counts as sustainable."]], "1b.17"],
["Hanneke (45) takes out a term life insurance policy on the life of her husband Gert. She pays the premium from her own account. If Gert dies, the payout goes to Hanneke. Their daughter asks who has which role in this policy. What is correct?", [["Hanneke is policyholder and beneficiary, Gert is the insured", "Hanneke takes out the insurance, pays the premium and receives the payout. The risk of death concerns Gert, so he is the insured."], ["Gert is policyholder and insured, Hanneke is only beneficiary", "Hanneke concluded the contract, so she is the policyholder."], ["Hanneke is the insured, because she pays the premium", "The insured is the person on whose life the insurance is taken out: Gert."], ["Gert is the beneficiary, because the payout concerns his death", "On his death Gert receives nothing; the beneficiary is Hanneke."]], "1g.5"],
["On Saturday Tom buys a second-hand car and wants to drive it home the same day. The insurer has not yet assessed his application. His intermediary arranges that he is nevertheless covered until the insurer's decision. What is this cover called?", [["Provisional cover", "Provisional cover gives temporary cover while the insurer is still assessing the application. If the application is rejected, the provisional cover ends after a short period."], ["A cover note", "A cover note confirms that an insurance policy has been concluded, for example as proof as long as the policy is not yet available."], ["A grace period", "That is a period in which a premium arrear can still be paid before the cover lapses."], ["Premium-free continuation", "That is the continuation of a life insurance policy without further premium payments."]], "1g.6"],
["A client has a buildings insurance policy. Their gutter leaks through rust, as a result of which the gutter itself must be replaced. What does the law in principle provide about loss caused by an inherent defect of the insured object?", [["That loss is not compensated, unless otherwise agreed in the policy", "According to the law, loss caused by an inherent defect is not eligible for compensation. A policy can arrange this differently, for example for consequential loss."], ["That loss is always compensated in full, because the object is insured", "The law in fact excludes loss caused by an inherent defect, unless otherwise agreed."], ["That loss is only compensated if the client already knew about the defect", "Knowledge of the defect does not make compensation more likely."], ["That loss is compensated through the insurer by the manufacturer", "The insurer does not settle loss on behalf of the manufacturer; the inherent defect is excluded by law."]], "1g.13"],
["Wendy (38) loses her job and does not pay the renewal premium on her car insurance. The insurer sends her a reminder. A few days later she is in a collision. She asks whether she is still covered and what happens if she does not pay. What is correct?", [["She is still covered: suspension is only allowed 14 days after the reminder without payment", "With a renewal premium the cover may only be suspended if payment is not made within 14 days of the reminder. Even with suspension Wendy remains liable for the premium."], ["She is not covered, because the cover lapses as soon as the premium is not paid on the due date", "With a renewal premium a reminder is needed first, with a period of 14 days."], ["She is covered, and if she does not pay the cover simply continues until the end of the year", "After a reminder and 14 days without payment the insurer can suspend the cover."], ["She is not covered, because an unemployed person may not have car insurance", "Unemployment has no influence on the cover; it is about the payment of the premium."]], "1g.23"],
["Gerrit (58) and Joke (56) want to know what their wealth position looks like. Their home is worth €420,000.00 and their mortgage is €180,000.00. They have €35,000.00 in savings and a car worth €15,000.00. In addition they have a revolving credit with a debt of €10,000.00. How large is their net worth?", [["€280,000.00", "Total assets are €470,000.00: home, savings and car. After deducting the debts of €190,000.00, mortgage and credit, €280,000.00 remains."], ["€290,000.00", "Here the revolving credit of €10,000.00 has not been counted as a debt."], ["€470,000.00", "This is the total of the assets, without deduction of the debts."], ["€265,000.00", "Here the car has not been counted as an asset."]], "2b.2"],
["Sophie Meijer (36) wants to invest €300.00 a month for later and asks for investment advice. She indicates that at least half of her investments must be sustainable within the meaning of the SFDR. Her adviser Tom establishes that no product in his offering meets that. Tom would still like to keep Sophie as a client. What is correct?", [["Tom recommends no product as suitable for that preference; Sophie may possibly adjust her preference", "A product that does not meet the sustainability preference may not be recommended as suitable for that preference. If Sophie knowingly adjusts her preference, Tom records this."], ["Tom recommends a non-sustainable product without saying so, because the preference is not binding", "Sustainability preferences are part of the suitability assessment and may not be ignored."], ["Tom describes an existing product in his advice report as sustainable, so that it fits after all", "That is misleading and a form of greenwashing."], ["Tom disregards the preference, because sustainability does not have to be part of advice", "In investment advice the adviser must in fact ask about sustainability preferences and take them into account."]], "1f.15"],
["The firm De Vries Assurantiën in Zwolle has twelve employees and an AFM licence for advising and intermediating in non-life insurance. The firm works with an online advice system from an external supplier and keeps all client files in the cloud. A new colleague has read that since 17 January 2025 the European DORA regulation applies to the financial sector. She asks whether the firm now has to meet all the DORA requirements. What is correct?", [["DORA does not apply to this firm, but the Wft requirement of controlled business operations does apply to ICT risks", "Insurance intermediaries that are a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise fall outside DORA. Controlled and ethical business operations, including around ICT and outsourcing, remain a Wft requirement."], ["DORA applies to every firm with an AFM licence, so the firm must meet all the requirements", "DORA has exceptions: small and medium-sized insurance intermediaries do not fall under it."], ["DORA only applies if the firm keeps the client files on its own servers", "Where the data is kept does not determine whether DORA applies; it is about the type and size of the institution."], ["DORA only applies once the Dutch legislature has transposed the regulation into national law", "An EU regulation has direct effect and does not need to be transposed; DORA has applied since 17 January 2025."]], "1f.33"]
];
